[{"section": "dev", "slug": "architecture", "text": "# Architecture\n\nBonkscape is a BepInEx 6 IL2CPP plugin for Megabonk (Unity 2023.2.22f1, IL2CPP, build 1.0.69) that reads the player's\nOld School RuneScape cache at run time. Nothing from either game is shipped. Written against **0.1.20** (`782ce3f`).\n\n## Projects\n\n| Path | What it is | Target |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/Bonkscape.Cache` | OSRS cache library: reads the cache and turns it into plain data (meshes as triangle soup, ARGB pixels, PCM samples). No Unity references. | net6.0 |\n| `src/Bonkscape.Plugin` | The BepInEx plugin (`Bonkscape.dll`): Harmony patches, systems, HUD. Compiles its game code only when Megabonk's interop assemblies are found (`INTEROP` define). | net6.0 |\n| `src/Bonkscape.Tools` | `bonk.exe`: preflight and code generation, plus cache inspection and map tools. | net8.0 |\n| `tools/package.py` | Builds `dist/Bonkscape-<version>.zip` from the Release build. | Python 3 |\n| `tools/sketch` | Map sketch tool (Leaflet page + `server.py`, port 8790): the OSRS world map from your cache, for outlining future maps. | Python 3 |\n| `tools/wiki-site` | This wiki's local site (port 8791) and `gen_tables.py`. | Python 3 |\n| `tools/hub` | [The hub](hub.md) (port 8789): one page that starts, stops and links the wiki and the sketch tool and renders the other docs; `Bonkscape Hub.cmd` in the repo root launches it. `export_wiki.py` writes BSWiki as a static site for hosting. | Python 3 |\n| `sheets/*.json` | The design data: the source of truth. | |\n| `docs/` | `MODLOG.md` (versions, workflow, numbered gotchas), `preflight.md` (generated report), `wiki/`, `dev/`. | |\n\nNot in git: `lib/` (BepInEx assemblies), `derived/` (renders and map tiles made from the cache), `dist/` (release zips),\n`bin/`, `obj/`.\n\n### Cache library (`src/Bonkscape.Cache`)\n\n| File | Does |\n|---|---|\n| `DiskStore.cs` | Opens `main_file_cache.dat2` and the `.idx` files (shared, read-only), reads a group's raw container bytes. `LooksLikeCache` tests a folder. |\n| `Container.cs`, `BZip2.cs` | Decompresses a container (none / bzip2 / gzip). |\n| `ReferenceTable.cs` | Index 255 reference tables: groups, files, name hashes, revisions. |\n| `OsrsCache.cs` | The cache API: `Config(group, id)`, `File(index, group, file)`, `HasGroup`, `FindGroup(name)`, `Table`, and `CandidateFolders`/`FindCacheFolder` (where to look). |\n| `JBuffer.cs` | Jagex big-endian buffer reads (smart ints, strings). |\n| `Defs.cs`, `Defs2.cs` | `NpcDef`, `ItemDef`, `ObjectDef`, `SpotAnimDef`, `IdentKitDef`, `TextureDef` decoders. |\n| `Port/ModelPort.cs` | RuneLite's `ModelLoader`/`ModelDefinition` ported mechanically (BSD-2-Clause, see `LICENSES/`). |\n| `OsrsMesh.cs` | Builds `MeshData` for NPCs, items, objects, spot animations and players (kits + worn items), with recolours, retextures, the client's lighting (`Model.light`) and Jagex HSL to RGB. |\n| `Anim.cs` | Frames and framemaps; applies the first frame of a stand sequence so models don't T-pose. |\n| `SpotAnimFrames.cs` | Renders a spot animation (model + sequence, e.g. 199, the level-up fireworks) frame by frame into ARGB images from one fixed camera, with each frame's length, for 2D flipbooks. |\n| `Raster.cs` | Software rasteriser: item inventory icons (`ItemIcon`, using the item's zoom/angles/offsets) and previews. |\n| `Sprites.cs`, `OsrsFont.cs` | Sprite groups and OSRS bitmap fonts (`p11_full`, `p12_full`, `b12_full`, `q8_full`). |\n| `SoundEffect.cs` | OSRS sound effect synthesiser (index 4 instruments) to 22,050 Hz PCM. |\n| `World/Region.cs` | Map regions: current caches' unnamed groups (`x << 8 \\| y`, file 0 terrain, file 1 objects) and older named `m{x}_{y}`/`l{x}_{y}` files; procedural heights. |\n| `World/WorldBuilder.cs` | Builds an area: terrain meshes, object meshes, wall meshes in 8x8-tile cells, collision boxes, tile flags (blocked, water, roofed, solid, bridge), wall edges, and named objects to track (trees, rocks). |\n| `World/Minimap.cs` | Renders an area like the client's minimap. |\n\n## Load sequence (`Plugin.Load`)\n\n1. `Settings.Load()` reads `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\settings.properties` (`OSRS_DIR`, `OSRS_CACHE`).\n2. Config keys are bound (`BepInEx/config/gg.melty.bonkscape.cfg`); a non-empty `OSRS.CacheFolder` overrides\n   `OSRS_CACHE`; prayer keys are parsed.\n3. `Rows.Build()` (lookups over phase-1 rows), `Bonk.Init()` (Lumbridge's `EMap` from `maps.bonk_base_map`),\n   `Skills.Load()`, `Hud.Init()` (subscribes to XP drop and level-up events), `TestMode.Init()` (reads Melty's test file).\n4. `OsrsCache.FindCacheFolder()`. None found: `CacheMissing`, and `osrs-cache` is reported failed in test mode.\n   Found: `Osrs.Start(folder)` starts the background build.\n5. `Harmony.PatchAll` over the assembly ([patch list](#harmony-patches)).\n6. `OsrsAudio` is registered as an IL2CPP type; the `Runner` MonoBehaviour is added.\n\n## The background asset build (`Core/Osrs.cs`)\n\nA background thread (`Bonkscape cache`, below-normal priority) decodes everything into plain data, so Megabonk's menus\nstay responsive. Unity objects are only made later, on the main thread, by `UnityConv`.\n\n| Step (`Osrs.Status`) | What |\n|---|---|\n| `enemies` | Each phase-1 enemy row: its NPC, then each `osrs_npc_alternates` id (if `UseStandIns`), first that builds. |\n| `players` | Each adventurer from kits + worn items in the stand pose; retried without worn items whose models are missing. |\n| `items` | Meshes and inventory icons for weapons, passives, drops and evolutions, and every coin stack variant of item 995. |\n| `sprites` | Weapon/evolution icon sprites, prayer icons and overheads, skill icons, UI sprites; fonts. |\n| `objects` | Map props, skilling node objects, fishing spot NPCs. |\n| `sounds` | Weapon, prayer and audio-row sound effects, synthesised. |\n| `ready` | `Ready = true`, summary logged, missing assets logged. Then, if `Map.RealLumbridge`, the arena. |\n\nThe arena build runs `WorldBuilder.Build` over `maps.lumbridge.osrs_area` (tracking objects named Tree, Oak and Rocks),\ngives up if any region is missing, renders the minimap and hands both to `Systems.Arena`.\n\nTextured faces are coloured with their texture's average colour (`Osrs.TextureColor`); everything is drawn with one\nunlit vertex-colour material (`Hidden/Internal-Colored`).\n\n## How sheets become code\n\n```\nsheets/*.json \u2500\u2500\u25ba bonk preflight \u2500\u2500\u25ba docs/preflight.md            (report: open items by phase)\n                        \u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500\u25ba sheets/cache_assets.json     (every OSRS asset the sheets use, generated)\n                        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Generated/Sheets.g.cs   (one class per sheet, one object per row)\n```\n\n`Codegen` infers each column's C# type across the rows (int, float, bool, string, arrays); nested objects and mixed\narrays stay as compact JSON text, which the plugin reads with `Core/Json.cs`. `Core/Rows.cs` builds lookups over the\n**phase-1 rows only** (by id, by Megabonk base, by style), so phase-2/3 rows never reach the game. See\n[Sheets reference](sheets-reference.md).\n\nThe plugin applies the rows to Megabonk's own data in the `DataManager.Load` postfix (`Systems/Content.cs`):\n\n- **Weapons**: base stats, `baseStats` entries and the upgrade pool of each `bonk_base` `WeaponData`; names.\n- **Tomes**: each passive's stat modifier, level description and name.\n- **Enemies**: HP/damage/speed/knockback for non-miniboss, non-boss bases, added to the Lumbridge map; unmapped\n  enemies removed from it; the timeline's start enemies, unlock times and swarm contents from `waves`.\n- **Characters**: stat modifiers, name, description and starting weapon (by skill levels).\n- **Map**: the name.\n\nIcons and tome descriptions are written into Megabonk's data fields once the cache is decoded (`Content.ApplyIcons`),\nbecause Harmony can't call the original of an IL2CPP virtual method ([Gotchas](gotchas.md#il2cpp-and-harmony)).\n\n## Run lifecycle (`Core/Runner.cs`)\n\n`Runner` is the per-frame driver. A run is \"active\" while `Bonk.Active` is true: Megabonk's current map is the\nLumbridge map (`EMap.Forest`) and it isn't the main menu.\n\n**Every frame (`Update`):**\n\n1. Once: log which shaders exist; when the cache is ready and the data applied, `Content.ApplyIcons()` and pass\n   `osrs-cache`.\n2. `TestMode.Tick`, `OsrsAudio.EnsureAttached` (keeps the mixer on the current AudioListener).\n3. Stage start: when active and `MyPlayer.Instance` exists and is a new object (first stage, or a new stage), `OnStage`.\n4. Run end: when active turns false, `OnRunEnd`.\n5. While active: the props/arena timer, `Arena.TryBuild` until it succeeds, `Arena.Tick`, `Pathing.Tick`,\n   `Prayer.Tick`, `Skills.GameTick`, `Loot.Tick`, `Skilling.Tick`, death detection.\n6. Always: `Skills.Tick` (autosave every 20 s), `Hud.Tick` (skipped when `Debug.OsrsHud` is off; hitsplats, XP drops, health bar timers, dialogues,\n   `LevelUpFx.Tick`; outside a run `MegabonkHud.Restore` puts back the Megabonk HUD pieces it hid), `Chat.Tick`.\n\n**`LateUpdate`** (while active): `EnemySkins.LateTick` (models follow enemies, Megabonk renderers stay hidden, hitbox\nfloor, `Bosses.Tick`), `Arena.LateTick` (see-through walls), `PlayerSkin.LateTick`.\n\n**`OnGUI`**: `Hud.OnGUI` (missing-cache message, the run HUD, or the character select panel; skipped when\n`Debug.OsrsHud` is off). Once the cache is ready\nit starts `OsrsUi.EnsureLoaded` (the HUD's interface sprites and the `q8_full` font, on a background thread). The run\nHUD calls `MegabonkHud.Tick` when `Debug.HideMegabonkHud` is on (finds Megabonk's `HealthUI` and `XpBarUI` every 1.5 s\nand hides them; off, the XP bar is never found, so `MegabonkHud.XpProgress` returns -1), places its blocks\nwith `HudLayout.Arrange` against Megabonk's minimap (`OsrsUi.Minimap`: measured from `MinimapUi.border`'s corners,\nretried every 2 s, else estimated) and draws them through `OsrsUi`.\n\n**`OnStage(player)`**: on the first stage of a run, resets the run clock, prayer, evolutions, loot and chat, and posts\nthe welcome line. Every stage: `Sizing.Measure`, `CameraTweak.Apply`, `PlayerSkin.Apply` (if not skinned yet),\n`Skilling.SpawnForRun` (Forest-style nodes around the player, replaced if the arena builds), a 1.5 s timer, and\n`Hud.FindGoldCounter` (also clears health bars, XP drops and the minimap measurement for the new stage).\n\nWhen the 1.5 s timer runs out: if the arena is available, `Arena.TryBuild` is called every frame until Megabonk's\nspawn intro has settled (or 8 s pass); otherwise `MapProps.Reskin` dresses the Forest.\n\n**`OnRunEnd`**: saves skills, clears skilling, props, arena, pathing, loot, prayer, the player model and enemy models.\n**`OnApplicationQuit`**: saves skills. Exceptions in each callback are caught; the first 20 are logged.\n\n## The arena pipeline (`Systems/Arena.cs`)\n\n1. **Measure**: `Sizing.Measure(player)`; the arena's scale is `Sizing.MetresPerUnit` (Megabonk character height x\n   `AdventurerScale` / adventurer height in OSRS units).\n2. **Hide the Forest**: every root object with a collider or mesh renderer is switched off (colliders and renderers\n   disabled, remembered for restore) unless it holds the player, enemies, cameras, pickups, interactables (chests,\n   shrines, the boss portal), UI, or is `WorldCollider`/`WorldEdgeTop`/`PlayerCamera`. The procedural tile roots and\n   the grass renderer go too.\n3. **Place Lumbridge**: a root object centred on Megabonk's `MapEdges` centre (captured by a `MapEdges.Set` prefix),\n   with the spawn tile's ground at the adventurer's feet.\n4. **Meshes**: terrain on Megabonk's ground layer (8) with `MeshCollider`s; objects and wall cells on layer 0.\n5. **Colliders**: `WorldData.Boxes` (walls, big scenery, trunks, water) as `BoxCollider`s on a **free physics layer**\n   (the highest unnamed layer from 31 down to 16), set to collide with the player's and the enemy layer. Megabonk's\n   camera (1\\|8\\|12), spawn raycasts (ground\\|object) and projectiles don't test that layer.\n6. **Spawn bounds**: `SpawnPositions.FindBounds` is re-run; its postfix sets `minX..maxZ` to the arena minus 2 tiles.\n7. **Minimap**: Megabonk's `MinimapMesh` renderers off; a textured quad with Lumbridge's minimap on the minimap layer.\n   `Minimap.Render(..., separateIcons: true)` returns the map scene and map function icons separately; they're packed\n   into one atlas and drawn as one mesh of quads, which `UpdateIcons` turns every frame to face Megabonk's minimap\n   camera, so icons stay upright. `Minimap.Zoom` divides that camera's `orthographicSize`.\n8. **Move in**: `TeleportPlayerImmediate` to the spawn tile facing west, then `rb.position` and the transform, repeated\n   for 2 s in `Arena.Tick` ([Gotchas](gotchas.md#megabonk-runtime)).\n9. **Interactables**: chests and shrines to random open tiles; the `InteractableBossSpawner` to `boss_tile`.\n10. **Enemies** already alive are teleported to the player; **skilling spots** are placed on tracked trees, rocks and\n    shore tiles.\n11. `lumbridge-arena` passes. Any exception: clear Lumbridge and restore the Forest.\n\nEach frame afterwards, `Arena.Tick` catches falls (25 m under the lowest ground: back to the courtyard), and\n`Arena.LateTick` turns the minimap icons and hides wall cells whose bounds cross the ray from `PlayerCamera`'s camera\nto the adventurer (logging a camera/wall summary every 20 s). `Pathing` searches the tile grid\nfrom the adventurer every 0.5 s or on a tile change, and an `EnemyMovementRb.GetTargetPosition` postfix aims each\nmonster at its next tile.\n\n## Harmony patches\n\nEverything Bonkscape patches, from the code (`[HarmonyPatch]` in `src/Bonkscape.Plugin`). The `hooks` column names the\nmatching row in `sheets/hooks.json`; **\"none\"** means the sheet has no row, so the preflight never checks that the\ntarget still exists ([docket](docket.md)).\n\n| Target | Kind | File | What it does | `hooks` row |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `SteamLeaderboardsManagerNew.QueueLeaderboardUpload` | prefix (skip) | Patches/CorePatches | Modded runs never queue leaderboard scores | `leaderboard_queue` |\n| `SteamLeaderboardsManagerNew.UploadLeaderboardScore` | prefix (skip) | Patches/CorePatches | ...or upload them | `leaderboard_upload` |\n| `DataManager.Load` | postfix | Patches/CorePatches | Applies the sheets to Megabonk's data; optional data dump | `data_loaded` |\n| `DeathScreen.StartDeathScreen` | postfix | Patches/CorePatches | \"Oh dear, you are dead!\" title; death message timer; test mode keeps the screen | `death_screen` |\n| `UnlockableBase.GetName` | prefix (replace) | Systems/Content | OSRS names for weapons, tomes, characters, the map; reimplements the localized name otherwise | `names` |\n| `EnemyData.GetName` | prefix | Systems/Content | OSRS monster names | none |\n| `StageData.GetName` | prefix | Systems/Content | Stage names: Lumbridge & Swamp, Lumbridge Swamp, Lumbridge Swamp Caves | none |\n| `UnlockUtility.GetAvailableWeapons` | postfix | Systems/Content | Level-up weapon offers: only Bonkscape weapons (in Lumbridge) | `weapon_pool` |\n| `UnlockUtility.GetAvailableTomes` | postfix | Systems/Content | Tome offers: only gear passives, one per slot, below max level | `tome_pool` |\n| `MyAchievements.IsUnlocked(UnlockableBase, out string)` | postfix | Systems/Content | Bonkscape weapons, tomes and characters count as unlocked | none |\n| `Enemy.InitEnemy` | postfix | Systems/EnemySkins | OSRS model, size tier, hide Megabonk's renderer (re-sized in `LateTick` once the hitbox is live) | `enemy_spawn` |\n| `Enemy.ReleaseToPool` | postfix | Systems/EnemySkins | Hide the model of a pooled enemy | none |\n| `Enemy.DamageFromPlayerWeapon` | prefix + postfix | Systems/Combat | HP before/after: hitsplat and skill XP for damage dealt | `enemy_damaged` |\n| `Enemy.EnemyDied(DamageContainer)` | postfix | Systems/Combat | Kill count, prayer potion drops, `osrs-enemy-killed` | `enemy_died` |\n| `DamageNumbers.SetDamage(float, Color, Vector3, int)` | postfix | Systems/Combat | Blank Megabonk's damage numbers in Lumbridge | `damage_numbers` |\n| `DamageNumbers.SetDamage(string, Color, Vector3, int)` | postfix | Systems/Combat | Blank Megabonk's \"-N\" player damage text | none (covered by `damage_numbers` in spirit) |\n| `PlayerHealth.Damage` | prefix | Systems/Prayer | Protection prayers reduce or cancel damage by monster style; player hitsplat | `player_damage` |\n| `PickupManager.SpawnPickup` | postfix | Systems/Loot | Coins and food wear OSRS item models | `pickup_spawn` |\n| `Pickup.ApplyPickup` | prefix + postfix | Systems/Loot | Food heals by its row; pickup sounds; `osrs-item-picked` | `pickup_apply` |\n| `InteractableChest.Start` | postfix | Systems/Loot | Chests wear the OSRS casket | `chest_spawn` |\n| `MoneyFlying.Set` | postfix | Systems/Loot | Flying coins wear the OSRS coin stack | none |\n| `MoneyFlying.Pickup` | postfix | Systems/Loot | Coin sound (rate-limited), `osrs-item-picked` | none |\n| `InteractableChest.OpenChestImplementation` | postfix | Systems/Evolutions | Try evolutions | `chest_open` |\n| `PlayerRenderer.SetCharacter` | postfix | Systems/PlayerSkin | The OSRS adventurer model | `player_model` |\n| `MapEdges.Set` | prefix | Systems/Arena | Remember the stage centre | none |\n| `SpawnPositions.FindBounds` | postfix | Systems/Arena | Spawn bounds onto Lumbridge | none |\n| `EnemyMovementRb.GetTargetPosition` | postfix | Systems/Pathing | Aim monsters at their next tile on the grid | none |\n| `PlayerInput.MovementInput` | postfix | Systems/TestMode | Autoplay movement (test mode only) | none |\n\nPolled or called, not patched: `MyPlayer.Instance` (stage start, `run_started`), `RandomObjectPlacer` output after\ngeneration (`map_props`), `KillsAndGoldCounter.t_gold` (hidden, `gold_hud`), `UpgradeButton.SelectUpgrade` and\n`BaseEncounterWindow.ChooseOffer` (autoplay), `MapController.StartNewMap` (autoplay start), `PlayerCamera.offset3rdPerson`\nand `maxExtraZoomoutDistance` (camera distance), the minimap camera's `orthographicSize` (`Minimap.Zoom`), `MoneyUtility.SpawnMoney` and `statusEffects.TestPickup` (skilling),\n`HealthUI`, `XpBarUI` (hidden in a run; `desiredRatio` read for the XP counter's strip), `EnemyHpBar` (scanned every\n0.5 s in a run and hidden; a Harmony patch on `EnemyHpBar.Set` in 0.1.17 went with a crash), `MinimapUi.border` (measured\nfor the minimap frame) and the active ability's `GetCooldown`/`readyAtTime` (the special attack orb).\n\nRows in `hooks.json` with **no patch** in the code: `icons_weapon`, `icons_tome`, `icons_character` (icons are written\ninto data fields instead), `music` (`MusicController.PlayMusicTrack`: no music synthesiser yet) and `timer`\n(`GameManager.GetAliveTime`: the OSRS clock was removed in 0.1.7). The sheet as it stands:\n\n<!-- gen:hooks -->\n| Hook | System | Target | Kind | Purpose | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `leaderboard_queue` | safety | `SteamLeaderboardsManagerNew.QueueLeaderboardUpload` | prefix | modded runs never queue leaderboard scores | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `leaderboard_upload` | safety | `SteamLeaderboardsManagerNew.UploadLeaderboardScore` | prefix | modded runs never upload leaderboard scores | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `data_loaded` | data | `DataManager.Load` | postfix | apply weapons/passives/enemies/characters/maps/waves rows to Megabonk's ScriptableObjects | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `weapon_pool` | data | `UnlockUtility.GetAvailableWeapons` | postfix | level-up picks offer only Bonkscape weapons | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `tome_pool` | data | `UnlockUtility.GetAvailableTomes` | postfix | level-up picks offer only gear passives | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `names` | presentation | `UnlockableBase.GetName` | prefix | OSRS names for reskinned weapons, tomes and characters | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `icons_weapon` | presentation | `WeaponData.GetIcon` | prefix | OSRS item icons rendered from the cache | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `icons_tome` | presentation | `TomeData.GetIcon` | prefix | OSRS gear icons rendered from the cache | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `icons_character` | presentation | `CharacterData.GetIcon` | prefix | character portraits rendered from the OSRS player model | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `enemy_spawn` | enemies | `Enemy.InitEnemy` | postfix | swap the enemy's mesh for its OSRS NPC model, add style marker | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `enemy_damaged` | combat | `Enemy.DamageFromPlayerWeapon` | postfix | OSRS hitsplats and skill XP from damage dealt | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `enemy_died` | combat | `Enemy.EnemyDied` | postfix | kill counting, prayer potion drops, test check | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `player_damage` | prayer | `PlayerHealth.Damage` | prefix | protection prayers cut damage by enemy style | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `damage_numbers` | presentation | `DamageNumbers.SetDamage` | prefix | hide Megabonk's floating numbers where an OSRS hitsplat shows instead | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `pickup_spawn` | loot | `PickupManager.SpawnPickup` | postfix | coins and food pickups wear OSRS item models | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `pickup_apply` | loot | `Pickup.ApplyPickup` | postfix | food heals, item pickup sound and test check | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `chest_spawn` | loot | `InteractableChest.Start` | postfix | chests wear the OSRS casket model | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `chest_open` | loot | `InteractableChest.OpenChestImplementation` | postfix | evolutions open from caskets | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `player_model` | presentation | `PlayerRenderer.SetCharacter` | postfix | the player becomes their OSRS adventurer model | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `level_up` | presentation | `UpgradeButton.SelectUpgrade` | call (test mode) | test autoplay presses the first level-up offer; Megabonk's level-ups otherwise stay as they are | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `timer` | presentation | `GameManager.GetAliveTime` | poll | run timer drawn in OSRS's font from Megabonk's run time | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `death_screen` | presentation | `DeathScreen.StartDeathScreen` | postfix | Oh dear, you are dead! | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `music` | audio | `MusicController.PlayMusicTrack` | prefix | OSRS music per map when it decodes, else Megabonk's | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `run_started` | systems | `MyPlayer.get_Instance` | poll | a Lumbridge stage begins when Megabonk's player exists on the Lumbridge map: reset prayer, place skilling nodes, start test mode | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `map_props` | map | `RandomObjectPlacer.Generate` | poll | after the stage generates, Megabonk's trees, rocks and bushes are drawn with OSRS scenery models (their colliders stay) | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `gold_hud` | presentation | `KillsAndGoldCounter.t_gold` | data row | Megabonk's gold number and icon are hidden; the OSRS coin stack for the amount is drawn instead | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n<!-- /gen:hooks -->\n\n## Systems at a glance\n\n| File | System |\n|---|---|\n| `Systems/Bonk.cs` | Is this a Bonkscape run? (`Active`) |\n| `Systems/Content.cs` | Sheets into Megabonk's data; names, icons, level-up pools, unlocks, starting weapons |\n| `Systems/Arena.cs` | The real Lumbridge |\n| `Systems/Pathing.cs` | Tile-grid pathing for monsters |\n| `Systems/MapProps.cs` | Forest fallback: OSRS scenery on Megabonk's props |\n| `Systems/EnemySkins.cs` | OSRS monster models, size tiers |\n| `Systems/Bosses.cs` | The Giant Mole's dig |\n| `Systems/PlayerSkin.cs` | The OSRS adventurer model |\n| `Systems/CameraTweak.cs` | `Camera.Distance` |\n| `Systems/Combat.cs` | Damage dealt, kills, Megabonk damage numbers |\n| `Systems/Prayer.cs` | Protection prayers |\n| `Systems/Skills.cs` | Persistent skills, XP table, combat level |\n| `Systems/Skilling.cs` | Trees, rocks, fishing spots |\n| `Systems/Loot.cs` | Coins, food, caskets, prayer potions |\n| `Systems/Evolutions.cs` | Evolutions on casket open |\n| `Systems/Hud.cs`, `Chat.cs`, `CharacterSelect.cs` | The OSRS HUD: what to show, from the game's state |\n| `Systems/HudLayout.cs` | The HUD's layout and drawing from OSRS's interfaces (160 orbs, 122 XP counter, 162 chatbox, 233 level-up dialogue, 541 prayer book, 161 minimap frame), sprite ids in `UiSprite`. No Unity: also compiled into `bonk.exe` for `uisprites mock`. |\n| `Systems/OsrsUi.cs` | IMGUI canvas for `HudLayout`; loads its sprites and fonts; measures Megabonk's minimap |\n| `Systems/MegabonkHud.cs` | Hides Megabonk's health bars, XP bar and enemy health bars in a run and restores them after; reads run XP progress and the ability cooldown |\n| `Systems/LevelUpFx.cs` | OSRS level-up fireworks (spot animation 199) as a flipbook at the adventurer's feet |\n| `Systems/Sfx.cs`, `Core/OsrsAudio.cs` | OSRS sounds through an `OnAudioFilterRead` mixer |\n| `Systems/TestMode.cs` | Melty test mode and autoplay ([Testing](testing.md)) |\n| `Core/Sizing.cs` | One yardstick: adventurer height, OSRS units to metres, monster tiers |\n| `Core/UnityConv.cs` | `MeshData`/pixels into Unity meshes, textures, objects (main thread) |\n| `Dev/DataDump.cs` | `Dev.DumpData`: Megabonk's data as JSON |\n\n## Tools (`bonk.exe`)\n\nRun from `src/Bonkscape.Tools`. Most commands find a cache like the plugin does, or use `BONK_CACHE`; outputs go under\n`BONK_OUT` (default the current folder).\n\n| Command | Does |\n|---|---|\n| `bonk preflight <sheets> <interopDir> <devCache> <playerCache\\|-> <genOut\\|-> <report>` | Checks the sheets, writes the report, `cache_assets.json` and the generated rows |\n| `bonk npcs <name...>` / `bonk items <name...>` / `bonk objects <name...>` | Find definitions by name, with model availability |\n| `bonk render npc\\|item\\|icon\\|object\\|spotanim\\|player <id> [yaw pitch]` | PNG renders |\n| `bonk sprites <id...>`, `bonk text <font> <text>`, `bonk sfx <id...>` | Sprites, font text, synthesised sounds as WAV |\n| `bonk uisprites sheet\\|pick\\|dump\\|info\\|iface\\|healthbar\\|hitsplat\\|spotanim\\|mock` | Interface sprites for the HUD: contact sheets, dumps, interface layouts, health bars, hitsplats, spot animation frames; `mock [w h]` draws the HUD layout into `mock_WxH.png` |\n| `bonk map ...`, `bonk world ...` | Top-down map renders and 3D previews of an area |\n| `bonk worldtiles ...` | Tile pyramids for the sketch tool (surface, underground, instances) |\n| `bonk worldscan`, `bonk revs` | Check every region decodes; index revisions |\n| `bonk locs x0 y0 x1 y1 <name>` | Placed objects by name in an area |\n| `bonk probe`, `bonk names`, `bonk rawcfg`, `bonk kits` | Low-level inspection |\n\n## Build and release\n\n```\ncd src/Bonkscape.Plugin && dotnet build -c Release\npython tools/package.py <version>      # dist/Bonkscape-<version>.zip: Bonkscape.dll, Bonkscape.Cache.dll, README, LICENSE, LICENSES/\n```\n\nThe plugin compiles against `lib/bepinex-melty` (BepInEx 6.0.0-be.697 from the game folder, the build Melty installs)\nand Megabonk's interop assemblies (`InteropLib`, default `D:\\Steam\\steamapps\\common\\Megabonk\\BepInEx\\interop`). Bump\n`Plugin.Version` for every build you upload. `package.py` runs the docs checker first and refuses to build the zip\nwhen it fails (`--skip-docs` for emergencies; [the docs checker](updating-docs.md#the-docs-checker)). Then upload, submit and test through Melty ([Testing](testing.md)), and\nupdate the docs ([How to update these docs](updating-docs.md)).\n\n<!-- sources: src/ tools/ -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "changelog", "text": "# Changelog and patch notes\n\nEvery Bonkscape version, newest first. Each entry has:\n\n- **Patch notes**: short and player-facing, safe to paste into a release.\n- **Changes**: what changed for developers, and where.\n- **Build**: when the zip was made (local time, UTC-5), the commit it was built from (the `1.0.0+<hash>` in the DLL;\n  the working tree can be ahead of it) and the commit that holds its code.\n- **Test**: the Melty test ([Testing](testing.md#test-history)).\n\nReconstructed from `git log`, `docs/MODLOG.md`, Melty's release list (changelog text and tests) and the strings\ninside each release's DLL in `dist/`. No version has been published yet: every release is a Melty draft.\n\n---\n\n## 0.1.20: monsters on the adventurer's scale\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 06:58, built from `6b33dbe`, code in `782ce3f`. Test `9634e18a`: running.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Monsters are drawn on your adventurer's own scale, so OSRS's proportions hold between everyone: a guard about as\n  tall as you, a goblin about two-thirds of that, a chicken about two-fifths.\n- `Models.MonsterSize` (1 = OSRS proportions) replaces `Models.MonsterScale`.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Sizing.MonsterMetresPerUnit` is `MetresPerUnit x Models.MonsterSize` (it was `MetresPerUnit / AdventurerScale x\n  MonsterScale`): monsters use the adventurer's OSRS-units-to-metres again. The tier ceilings are unchanged.\n- Config: `Models.MonsterScale` (1.0, 0.5 to 3) replaced by `Models.MonsterSize` (1.0, 0.3 to 3).\n- New `Debug.HideMegabonkHud` (`true`): off, `Hud` skips `MegabonkHud.Tick`, so Megabonk's health, XP and enemy bars\n  stay and its XP bar isn't read (`XpProgress` returns -1). It splits the 0.1.17/0.1.18 crash: the main session tests\n  0.1.20 with it off.\n- Model heights from the cache, as the main session measured them (OSRS units, standing model with the NPC\n  definition's width and height scale): Warrior 216, Guard 201, Cow 153, Giant Mole 150, Goblin 129, Giant rat 125,\n  Giant frog 85, Chicken 79.\n\n## 0.1.19: a switch for the OSRS HUD\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 06:52, built from `abfc90f`, code in `2445030`. Test `9f22aab1`: 1-run quick check, passed: no crash,\nall seven self-checks. The main session ran it with `Debug.OsrsHud=false`.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- New `Debug.OsrsHud` setting (on by default): off turns Bonkscape's OSRS HUD off and leaves Megabonk's HUD as it is.\n  For tracking down the crash at start in 0.1.17 and 0.1.18.\n\n**Changes**\n- New config key `Debug.OsrsHud` (`true`). Off, `Runner` skips `Hud.Tick` and `Hud.OnGUI`: no HUD drawing, no\n  `OsrsUi.EnsureLoaded` (interface sprites and the `q8_full` font), no `MegabonkHud` hiding. `Hud.Init` still\n  subscribes to XP drops and level-ups, so the chat line, the level-up sound, `xp-drop` and `LevelUpFx.Play` (which\n  renders the fireworks frames on a background thread) still run.\n\n## 0.1.18: no Harmony patch on enemy health bars\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 06:43, built from `d283a13`, code in `1bc777c`. Test `b09071b7`: 1 run, **failed**: the same crash\nin `coreclr.dll` (c0000005) 17 s in, before a run started; only `osrs-cache` reported.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Meant to fix 0.1.17's crash 18 seconds after the game started. It didn't: 0.1.18 crashes the same way.\n\n**Changes**\n- `MegabonkHud`: Megabonk's enemy health bars are pooled objects (`EffectManager.AttachEnemyHpBar`), now found with\n  `FindObjectsOfType<EnemyHpBar>` every 0.5 s during a run and hidden, instead of the Harmony postfix on\n  `EnemyHpBar.Set`. That patch was 0.1.17's only new native detour, and 0.1.17 crashed in `coreclr.dll` 18 s in (the\n  commit says as the first enemies spawned); 0.1.18's test crashed the same way, so it wasn't (or wasn't the only) cause.\n\n## 0.1.17: OSRS-styled HUD\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 06:37, built from `92fc0b6`, code in `d283a13`. Test `aebf6011`: 1 run, **failed**: Megabonk crashed\nin `coreclr.dll` (c0000005) 18 s in, before a run started; only `osrs-cache` reported.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- An OSRS HUD drawn from your cache's own interface art: hitpoints, prayer and special attack orbs beside the minimap,\n  an XP counter with the drops rising into it, and a prayer panel at the bottom right.\n- OSRS health bars over monsters you hit, and over your adventurer whenever you're hurt. Megabonk's own bars are\n  hidden in Lumbridge and come back on its other maps.\n- Level-ups show OSRS's level-up dialogue in the chat box and the level-up fireworks at your feet.\n- OSRS's minimap frame round Megabonk's minimap, with a compass that turns with the camera.\n\n**Changes**\n- New `Systems/HudLayout.cs` (no Unity; also compiled into `bonk.exe`): the layout from the cache's interfaces (160\n  orbs, 122 XP counter, 162 chatbox, 233 level-up dialogue, 541 prayer book, 161 minimap frame), sprite ids in\n  `UiSprite` (not rows in `sheets/ui.json`, so the preflight doesn't check them). HUD scale `round(height / 540)`,\n  the chatbox one step smaller.\n- New `Systems/OsrsUi.cs`: the IMGUI canvas; loads the interface sprites and the `q8_full` font on a background\n  thread once the cache is ready (log: `OSRS interface sprites loaded`); measures Megabonk's minimap from\n  `MinimapUi.border`'s corners (log: `minimap border corners ...`), else estimates it. The minimap frame and compass\n  are drawn only round a measured minimap; north is `Hud.NorthYaw` = 0 (Unity +z).\n- New `Systems/MegabonkHud.cs`: in a Lumbridge run hides `HealthUI` (HUD bar and the bar under the adventurer),\n  `XpBarUI`'s bar (its level text stays) and enemy health bars (new postfix on `EnemyHpBar.Set`, no `hooks` row);\n  restores them once `Bonk.Active` is false (log: `Megabonk HUD restored (N pieces)`). Reads `XpBarUI.desiredRatio`\n  and the active ability's cooldown for the special attack orb.\n- New `Systems/LevelUpFx.cs` and `Cache/SpotAnimFrames.cs`: spot animation 199 rendered to a flipbook on a\n  background thread (log: `level-up fireworks: N frames, S s`), drawn at the adventurer's feet on unscaled time.\n- `Hud.cs` rewritten around them (public API unchanged): health bars for 6 s after a hit (30/50/80 px by tier), the\n  adventurer's whenever hurt; level-ups open the dialogue for 3 s instead of a 2.2 s banner; `Hud.Banner`\n  (evolutions) shows as a dialogue. `CharacterSelect.cs` on an OSRS stone panel.\n- `bonk uisprites sheet|pick|dump|info|iface|healthbar|hitsplat|spotanim|mock`; `mock [w h]` draws the HUD layout\n  into a PNG. Design notes: `docs/design/ui-style.md`.\n\n## 0.1.16: autoplay opens chests\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 06:07, built from `1ab911b`, code in `d18cdb0`. Test `9e1854a7`: 1-run quick check, passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- No change for players: Melty's test autoplay now opens chests, so tests reach caskets and evolutions.\n\n**Changes**\n- `TestMode`: in a `ChestWindowUi`, autoplay presses Open, then Take about 3 s later; after 8 s a stuck window is\n  discarded and a warning is logged (which would fail Melty's `loader-errors` check, so a stuck chest shows up).\n\n## 0.1.15: OSRS proportions all the way, a closer minimap\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 05:59, built from `6e4df04`, code in `1ab911b`. Test `13a522b9`: 1-run quick check, passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Monsters keep OSRS proportions all the way: they no longer grow to fit Megabonk's oversized hitboxes.\n- The minimap is zoomed in towards OSRS's scale (new `Minimap.Zoom` setting, 2.5).\n\n**Changes**\n- `Models.HitboxFill` replaced by **`Models.MinHitboxShare`**, default **0** (off). Megabonk's enemy hitboxes are tall\n  capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton), so a hitbox floor undid OSRS proportions; the key was renamed because existing\n  configs kept 0.85.\n- New `Minimap.Zoom` (2.5, 1 to 6): divides the minimap camera's `orthographicSize`, following any size Megabonk sets.\n\n## 0.1.14: upright minimap icons\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 05:53, built from `a236431`, code in `6e4df04`. Test `77b7beb2`: 1-run quick check, passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Minimap icons (trees, rocks, map functions) stay upright as the minimap turns, like in OSRS.\n- Walls in the camera's way hide reliably.\n- Elites and minibosses grow only within their size limits once Megabonk enlarges them.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Minimap.Render(separateIcons)`: map scene and map function icons come back as icons; `Arena.BuildIcons` packs them\n  into one atlas mesh over Lumbridge's minimap, and `Arena.UpdateIcons` turns it to Megabonk's minimap camera every\n  frame.\n- Walls hide for `PlayerCamera`'s camera (`Camera.main` can be another camera); camera and wall diagnostics in the\n  log every 20 s.\n- `EnemySkins.FitHitbox`: Megabonk enlarges elites and minibosses after spawn, so the re-size happens when the hitbox\n  goes live, re-applying the capped enlargement; logs a `resize ...` line.\n\n## 0.1.13: monster sizes and a closer camera\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 05:41, built from `fe57644`, code in `a236431`. Test `2f85d870`: 1-run quick check, passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Your adventurer is now clearly bigger than ordinary monsters: monsters keep OSRS proportions against Megabonk's\n  character, not your enlarged adventurer (in the log: adventurer 4.8 m, guard 2.8 m, goblin 1.8 m, chicken 1.1 m).\n- Elites, minibosses and bosses grow only so far (bosses at most 2.2 times your height), so no more castle-sized cows.\n- Megabonk's follow camera sits closer (new `Camera.Distance` setting, 0.8).\n\n**Changes**\n- `Sizing`: `MonsterMetresPerUnit` (monsters at Megabonk-character scale x `MonsterScale`), `Tier` (normal, elite,\n  miniboss, boss), `MaxEnlarge` (1.15 / 1.4 / 1.6 / 2.0 of Megabonk's enlargement), `MaxHeight` (1.1 / 1.35 / 1.7 x\n  adventurer, bosses `Models.BossMaxHeight`), `AdventurerHeight` (set by `PlayerSkin`).\n- `EnemySkins`: tier from `IsBoss`/`IsStageBoss`/`IsFinalBoss`, `Miniboss*` names, `IsElite`; height capped; the\n  hitbox floor can't pass the cap; one log line per enemy type and tier.\n- `Models.HitboxFill` default 0.85 to **0.6**. New `Models.BossMaxHeight` (2.2) and `Camera.Distance` (0.8).\n- New `Systems/CameraTweak.cs`: scales `PlayerCamera.offset3rdPerson` (Megabonk's is about 11 m) and\n  `maxExtraZoomoutDistance` (about 15 m) once per camera, from Megabonk's values; applied every stage.\n\n## 0.1.12: playability pass\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 05:15, built from `179fbb4`, code in `fe57644`. Test `3e8c9d4c`: 1-run quick check, passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Monsters find their way around walls and over bridges in Lumbridge instead of getting stuck.\n- More room to run: only buildings, big scenery, tree trunks and water block you now. Fences, railings, hedges, gates\n  and small clutter don't.\n- Your adventurer, the monsters and Lumbridge are 1.6 times bigger (`Models.AdventurerScale`).\n- A prayer bar at the top right shows the three protection prayers with their keys, the active one framed, and\n  \"Protected!\" flashes when a prayer stops a hit.\n\n**Changes**\n- New `Systems/Pathing.cs`: breadth-first search from the adventurer's tile over the arena grid\n  (`WorldData.CanStep`: wall edges, water, big scenery; diagonals need both side steps), every 0.5 s or on a tile\n  change; `EnemyMovementRb.GetTargetPosition` postfix aims monsters at their next tile; direct chase within 3 steps.\n- `WorldBuilder.Classify`: only walls, 2x2+ scenery, thin tree trunks and water block; a list of open names (fence,\n  railing, hedge, gate, door, stairs, crates, barrels...).\n- `Models.PlayerFit` (1.0) **renamed** `Models.AdventurerScale`, default **1.6**. An old config's `PlayerFit` line is\n  ignored.\n- `Hud`: prayer bar with keys, active prayer framed in gold, `Hud.Protected()` and \"Protected!\", clearer 45-second hint.\n- Release README updated to the real-Lumbridge text (0.1.0 to 0.1.11 all shipped the first README). It still names\n  the setting `PlayerFit`, renamed in this version.\n- Between 0.1.11 and 0.1.12, not in the plugin: the map sketch tool (`tools/sketch`, `bonk worldtiles`, `0b799aa`,\n  `179fbb4`), `bonk worldscan`/`revs` (`6acb56c`), and the preflight against this PC's full RuneLite cache (143/143\n  phase-1 assets, `aee5241`).\n- Footage review noted the adventurer still read small (the world and monsters scaled with it), which 0.1.13 fixes.\n\n## 0.1.11: Lumbridge passes the publish test\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 03:56, built from `01a00f7`, code in `583d4bd`. Test `09ad9949`: **2 runs x 4 min, passed**, all\nseven self-checks, footage reviewed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- The real Lumbridge, built from your own OSRS cache: the castle, the River Lum and its bridges, the church, the swamp\n  and the fields, with Lumbridge's own minimap. Walls in the camera's way step aside.\n- Walls, scenery and water have a collision layer of their own, which you and the monsters bump into.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Arena.SolidLayer`: collision boxes on the highest unnamed physics layer, set to collide with the player's and the\n  enemy layer (they were on layer 0 in 0.1.10).\n- MODLOG gotchas 15 to 18 written. After the zip: README rewritten for the real Lumbridge (`fd15cc7`) and\n  `maps.lumbridge` marked verified (`3b27fb5`). The 0.1.11 zip still has the old README.\n\n## 0.1.10: see-through walls\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 03:51, built from `d1ffbc6`, code in `01a00f7`. Test `ce9989f6`: passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Walls between the camera and your adventurer step aside, so you can see where you're going.\n\n**Changes**\n- `WorldBuilder` emits wall meshes in 8x8-tile cells; `Arena.LateTick` hides cells whose bounds cross the\n  camera-to-adventurer ray.\n- Colliders moved off the camera's layers.\n- `EnemySkins.FitHitbox`: the hitbox floor is applied in `LateTick` once the collider is live.\n- Character size measured once.\n\n## 0.1.9: the ground holds\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 03:45, built from `97c29d6`, code in `d1ffbc6`. Test `531bf1f4`: passed, the first real-Lumbridge\nbuild to pass.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Fixed falling through Lumbridge's ground; monsters now spawn on it.\n\n**Changes**\n- `UnityConv`: triangles re-wound after the z flip, so terrain faces up (Unity mesh colliders and raycasts are\n  one-sided; ground collision and Megabonk's spawn raycasts went through backward ground).\n- Size measured once per run.\n\n## 0.1.8: moving into Lumbridge\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 03:41, built from `39bbd35`, code in `97c29d6`. Test `f9b58412`: failed (kill, pickup, prayer and\nXP checks never reported).*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- You now start in Lumbridge's castle courtyard reliably, and you're caught if you fall.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Arena.TryBuild` waits for Megabonk's spawn intro (on the ground, not teleporting, at most 8 s) before building.\n- The move sets the rigidbody position and transform, repeated for 2 s; falls 25 m below the lowest ground return you\n  to the courtyard.\n- `Sizing.Body` finds the character collider (`playerMovement.playerCollider`, then any upright collider).\n\n## 0.1.7: the real Lumbridge (first try)\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 03:36, built from `23ed7be`, code in `39bbd35`. Test `6c2d57ed`: failed (arena built; kill,\npickup, prayer and XP checks never reported).*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Lumbridge is now the real Lumbridge, built from your OSRS cache as the arena, in place of Megabonk's Forest with\n  OSRS trees.\n- Your adventurer matches Megabonk's character size; monsters keep OSRS proportions and stand on the ground.\n- A quieter HUD: no clock, a short chat box that hides itself, style icons only on the nearest monsters.\n\n**Changes**\n- Cache library: `World/Region` (current unnamed region groups and old `m`/`l` files, procedural heights),\n  `World/WorldBuilder` (terrain lit and coloured like the client, shaped overlays, objects rotated and mirrored like\n  `getModel`, collision boxes, bridges), `World/Minimap`.\n- `Systems/Arena`: hides the Forest, places Lumbridge on its ground/object layers, moves spawn bounds, the adventurer,\n  chests, shrines, the boss portal (swamp dark hole) and skilling spots; swaps the minimap. New self-check\n  `lumbridge-arena`.\n- `UnityConv` flips z (OSRS is right-handed; models were mirrored).\n- `Core/Sizing.cs`: the adventurer matches Megabonk's character; monsters keep OSRS proportions but never draw smaller\n  than their hitbox; feet on the ground. Config: `Models.Scale` replaced by `Models.PlayerFit` (1.0),\n  `Models.MonsterScale` (1.0), `Models.HitboxFill` (0.85); new `Map.RealLumbridge` (true).\n- `Hud`: no run clock, short chat box (8 s, repeats collapse), style markers on the nearest 10, 45-second key hint.\n- Sheets: `maps.osrs_area`, `spawn_tile`, `boss_tile`; the preflight builds the arena from both caches and checks\n  the tiles. Tools: `bonk world`, `bonk locs`; `bonk map` through the library.\n\n## 0.1.6: diagnostic build (not for players)\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 03:13, built from `23ed7be` with uncommitted probe code. Test `4038aeb7`: failed as expected (its\nprobe check never reported; the six normal checks passed).*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Not for players: a build that logs how Megabonk builds its stage and tests a replacement world.\n\n**Changes**\n- A stage probe: logged Megabonk's map generation (layers, masks, colliders, bounds, `MapEdges` centre, interactables)\n  and placed a test slab to see whether enemies reach it (`probe-enemies-on-slab`). What it found became MODLOG\n  gotcha 15. The probe code wasn't kept.\n- Included `81a3789`: Megabonk's own \"-N\" player damage text hidden (the OSRS hitsplat shows the hit); the test-mode\n  prayer potion boost stops after the first potion (autoplay was flooding the chat). Sheet statuses set; MODLOG\n  started.\n- `bonk map` (`23ed7be`): top-down renders of OSRS regions from the cache.\n\n## 0.1.5: first complete version\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 00:28, built from `2aca038`, code in `6febbfd`. Test `00b12845`: **2 runs x 4 min, passed**, all six\nself-checks, footage reviewed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Lumbridge & Swamp with OSRS monsters, scenery, adventurers, weapons, gear, prayers, skills, hitsplats, XP drops and\n  sound effects, all read from your own OSRS install.\n- The Giant Mole digs: it burrows and comes up next to you, more often when hurt.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Systems/Bosses.cs`: the Mole's dig from `bosses.attacks` (`burrow_teleport_every_12s`, 1.2 s telegraph, faster\n  below 50%).\n- Autoplay takes the first offer of shrine windows (`BaseEncounterWindow.ChooseOffer`).\n\n## 0.1.4: OSRS scenery, coins and the death screen\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 00:21, built from `2aca038`, code in `6febbfd`. Test `196b766b`: passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Megabonk's trees, rocks and bushes look like OSRS trees, rocks and bushes.\n- An OSRS coins counter, and \"Oh dear, you are dead!\".\n\n**Changes**\n- `Systems/MapProps.cs`: Megabonk's props drawn with OSRS scenery models after the stage generates (colliders kept).\n- `Hud`: OSRS coin stack in place of `KillsAndGoldCounter`'s number and icon; the OSRS-font run timer now reads\n  Megabonk's `GameManager.GetAliveTime`.\n- `DeathScreen.StartDeathScreen` postfix; autoplay restarts after death.\n- Run start keyed off `MyPlayer.Instance`; fishing spots use their OSRS NPC model.\n\n## 0.1.3: OSRS proportions\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 00:13, built from `7b77aa6`, code in `2aca038`. Test `a5e4376c`: passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Monsters and your adventurer have OSRS proportions.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Models.Scale` (1.15): OSRS models sized at 96 OSRS units per metre times the setting, times the enemy's scale.\n- Autoplay presses level-up offers (`UpgradeButton.SelectUpgrade`).\n- Commit `2aca038` holds all the in-game systems of 0.1.0 to 0.1.3, plus `README.md`, `LICENSE` and\n  `tools/package.py`.\n\n## 0.1.2: sizes and facing\n\n*Build 2026-10-21 00:07, built from `7b77aa6`. Test `212af9d8`: passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- OSRS models are sized and face the right way; coins look like OSRS coins.\n\n**Changes**\n- Model sizing against Megabonk's renderer height (logged per model).\n- The screenshot option removed (`ScreenCapture.CaptureScreenshot` is stripped in Megabonk's build).\n- Autoplay pick errors handled.\n\n## 0.1.1: the sound mixer\n\n*Build 2026-10-20 23:57, built from `7b77aa6`. Test `3d4554e1`: failed (\"Method unstripping failed\" errors).*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- OSRS sound effects play.\n\n**Changes**\n- `Core/OsrsAudio.cs`: sounds mixed into the output from `OnAudioFilterRead` on the AudioListener's object, because\n  `AudioClip.Create/SetData` are stripped. Renderer fixes for the IL2CPP build. The Melty test file's presence is logged.\n\n## 0.1.0: first playable build\n\n*Build 2026-10-20 23:47, built from `7b77aa6` with the in-game systems uncommitted. Test `f950c212`: failed (the\n`UnityConv` type initializer threw; no self-check reported).*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- First playable test build: Lumbridge & Swamp (Megabonk's Forest), OSRS monsters, adventurers, weapons, gear,\n  prayers, skills and HUD.\n\n**Changes**\n- Plugin systems: `Content` (sheets into Megabonk's data, names, level-up pools), `EnemySkins`, `PlayerSkin`,\n  `Combat`, `Prayer`, `Skills` (persistent, OSRS XP table), `Loot`, `Skilling`, `Evolutions`, `Hud`, `Chat`,\n  `CharacterSelect`, `TestMode` (Melty self-checks, autoplay), `Core/Osrs` (background decode), `Core/UnityConv`.\n- Config: `OSRS.CacheFolder`, `OSRS.UseStandIns`, `Dev.DumpData`, `Dev.AutoStartRun`, `Audio.OsrsVolume`,\n  `Prayer.Keys`, and a screenshot option.\n- Before it (`7b77aa6`, 23:24): `bonk preflight` and code generation, the sound synthesiser, stand-pose frames, player\n  models; phase-1 preflight clean.\n\n## 0.0.1: loader stub\n\n*Build 2026-10-20 22:46, before the first commit (its code is in `408476b`). Test `69badf81`: passed.*\n\n**Patch notes**\n- Development build: loads and finds your OSRS files; no gameplay changes yet.\n\n**Changes**\n- Stub plugin: reads `OSRS_DIR`/`OSRS_CACHE` from `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\settings.properties`, searches the cache\n  folders, logs what it found.\n- First commit (`408476b`, 23:13): the OSRS cache reader, the model and icon pipeline (RuneLite's model loader ported),\n  the design sheets and the stub plugin.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "docket", "text": "# Docket\n\nIdeas and tasks, grouped by milestone, in order. Statuses: <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span>\n<span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> <span class=\"st st-blocked\">blocked</span>.\nUpdate it with every version ([How to update these docs](updating-docs.md)). Last updated 2026-10-21, at 0.1.20.\n\nPhase 2/3 rows in the sheets are tracked by the sheets themselves (their `status`); this docket names them only where\na milestone needs them.\n\n## Current push\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Shared osrs-kit** | Started at `D:\\Modding\\osrs-kit`: shared RuneScape code, data dumps and docs. It will replace `src/Bonkscape.Cache`. Separate session. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Offline data and wiki dump** | Part of osrs-kit. The OSRS Wiki dump (2023-10-08, 135,796 pages) is set up: `python -I D:\\Modding\\osrs-kit\\tools\\wiki\\wiki.py` with `page`, `infobox`, `search` or `uses` (`--json` for scripts). **Check it before any live oldschool.runescape.wiki lookup** (the user's rule). |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Music research** | How OSRS music is stored and synthesised (MIDI tracks, patches, Vorbis samples). The user will pick one track per map. Session `music-research`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Map ideas and per-map music choices** | An Ideas layer in `tools/sketch` and `docs/design/`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **These wikis** | `docs/wiki`, `docs/dev`, this docket, `tools/wiki-site` (first version at 0.1.15). Keep them current with every version. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Monsters on the adventurer's scale** | 0.1.20 (`782ce3f`): the user asked that all OSRS humans be one scale and goblins scaled the same way, so monsters use the adventurer's OSRS-units-to-metres again (`Models.MonsterSize` replaces `MonsterScale`); tier ceilings unchanged. Test `9634e18a` running; check the sizes in its footage. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Monster sizing and camera** | 0.1.13 to 0.1.15: size tiers and ceilings, `Models.BossMaxHeight`, `Camera.Distance`, the hitbox floor off, `Minimap.Zoom` and upright minimap icons. 1-run quick tests passed. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Crash at start (0.1.17, 0.1.18)** | Tests `aebf6011`, `b09071b7` and `48b6a423`: Megabonk crashed in `coreclr.dll` (c0000005) 16 to 18 s in, while the Forest stage loads, 3 times out of 3; only `osrs-cache` reported. The main session's dump shows the main thread with a smashed stack, called from Megabonk's IL2CPP code into ours. Dropping the `EnemyHpBar.Set` patch (0.1.18) didn't fix it. 0.1.19 with `Debug.OsrsHud=false` ran clean (test `9f22aab1`), so it's in the new HUD code; 0.1.20 runs with `Debug.HideMegabonkHud=false` (HUD drawn, Megabonk's HUD left alone) to split it further (test `9634e18a` running). Once found, add the gotcha to `MODLOG.md`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **OSRS-faithful UI style pass** | The user wants the UI and look copied from OSRS as much as possible: real OSRS interface sprites from the cache, written up in `docs/design/ui-style.md`. Shipped in 0.1.17 (`d283a13`): minimap orbs, XP counter and drops, health bars, prayer panel, chatbox dialogues, level-up fireworks, minimap frame and compass; Megabonk's bars hidden in a run. Not confirmed in a run yet: 0.1.17 and 0.1.18 crashed at start; 0.1.19's test passed, but its footage hasn't been checked for the HUD. Session `osrs-ui-style`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Health bars over heads** | Requested by the user (2026-10-21). In 0.1.17: monsters for 6 s after a hit (30/50/80 px by tier), the adventurer whenever hurt. Not seen in a run yet. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Upright minimap icons, wall hiding, elite re-size** | 0.1.14 (`6e4df04`): map scene and map function icons drawn upright over Lumbridge's minimap; walls hide for Megabonk's player camera; elites and minibosses re-sized when Megabonk enlarges them after spawn. Quick test passed; keep an eye on wall hiding in footage. |\n\n## Next milestone: 0.2.0, animations\n\nThe 0.2 release is the one with animations (the user's call); until then versions stay 0.1.x. OSRS stand, walk,\nattack and death sequences for the adventurer and every monster, played in time with Megabonk.\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Sequence playback in the cache library** | `Anim.cs` only applies the first frame of a stand sequence. Needs every frame with its length, the framemaps, and a way to show it in Unity (baked meshes per frame, or vertex updates: `Mesh.vertices` isn't stripped). Do it in osrs-kit if it lands first. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Adventurer: stand, walk, run** | From the player's base animations (stand 808 is in `characters.osrs_player_model`). Walk/run chosen by Megabonk's move speed. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Monsters: stand and walk** | NPC definitions carry stand and walk sequence ids (`enemies.animation_ids` already plans `walk: from_npc_def`). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Monsters: attack and death** | Not in NPC definitions: needs the ids from the offline data (osrs-kit). Death plays before the model goes back to the pool (`Enemy.ReleaseToPool` timing). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Weapon-specific attack animations** | One sequence per weapon (whip, scimitar, shortbow, blowpipe, chinchompa, each spell, trident); add a column to `weapons`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Sync with Megabonk's attacks** | Find the hooks for \"the player's weapon fired\" and \"this enemy attacks\" so the sequence starts with the hit; add them to `hooks`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Giant Mole dig animation** | `enemies.giant_mole.animation_ids.dig`, with the existing dig timing. |\n\n## Then: character testing\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Each adventurer through autoplay runs** | `TestMode.StartRun` always picks the first `characters` row (Warrior). Choose by the test file's `run` or `seed` so Ranger and Mage get runs; then mark their rows verified. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Character select overlay** | The Bonkscape panel for each adventurer, at several resolutions, next to Megabonk's own character UI; portraits. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Sizing per adventurer** | `Sizing.Reset()` is never called, so Megabonk's character height is measured once per game session. Check switching adventurers between runs (`SirOofie`, `Robinette`, `Fox` colliders may differ). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Attack and Defence training** | The Warrior is aggressive (trains Strength); no adventurer trains Attack with its own weapon and none trains Defence. Decide: attack style choice, per-weapon styles, or the Ironman. |\n\n## Then: unlock systems and UI validation\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Gear requirements and starting weapons** | Every threshold (70 Attack, 55/75 Ranged, 75/94 Magic) with a prepared `skills.json`. Starting weapons are set only in the `DataManager.Load` postfix, but the panel computes them live: check whether a mid-session level-up needs a restart. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Skill XP and persistence** | XP per damage and per action, Hitpoints at a third, Prayer XP, save timing (20 s, run end, quit), unreadable-file recovery, the 200M cap. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Caskets and evolutions** | Both evolutions in one run (a test-mode shortcut to level 8 and the passive), stats restored at the next run, chat line and banner. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Gear slot rules** | Neck and ring exclusivity and the level-8 cap in the offers. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Level-up banners and chat** | Levels, repeats collapsing, chat box timing. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Every HUD element** | Hitsplats, minimap orbs, XP counter and drops, health bars, style icons, prayer panel, overhead, \"Protected!\", coins (K/M colours), level-up and evolution dialogues, fireworks, death text, missing-cache text, at 720p/1080p/1440p/4K. Unconfirmed from code alone: whether Megabonk's minimap gets measured (log `minimap border corners ...: used`), which way the compass turns (`Hud.NorthYaw`), and that Megabonk's HUD comes back after a run (log `Megabonk HUD restored`). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Prayer against minibosses** | Does Megabonk's `IsBoss()` count `MinibossPig`/`MinibossGolem`? That decides 100% or 50% blocking. |\n\n## Later\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **OSRS music synthesiser** | Built later, as part of osrs-kit, after the research. Unlocks one track per map (the user's picks), `maps.osrs_music_track`, `audio.lumbridge_music`, the level-up and death jingles. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Maps from the user's outlines, with music** | Outlines drawn in the sketch tool; each map a `maps` row with `osrs_area`, spawn, boss tile and music. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Underground and instance arenas** | Caves, dungeons and boss rooms (the sketch tool has underground and instance views). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **9-tile performance work** | For larger (3x3-region) maps: shared vertices, LOD, culling. Lumbridge is 16 regions as triangle soup today. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Switch Bonkscape to osrs-kit** | Replace `src/Bonkscape.Cache` with a reference to the shared kit once it covers what the plugin uses. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Phase 2 and 3 content** | Pure, Ironman, Dwarf multicannon, Dharok's, Scythe, AGS, Dragon claws, Fire cape, Godsword shards and their evolutions, special attacks, Barrows, the Wilderness, God Wars, the Fight Caves and Jad, pets, clue scrolls (see the sheets). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **OSRS projectiles and weapon sounds** | `weapons.osrs_projectile_or_spotanim_id` and `sfx_id`, and `audio.enemy_hit`/`kill`, are decoded or listed but never used. |\n\n## Recommended fixes and checks\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Monster hitbox floor** | Resolved in 0.1.15 (`1ab911b`): the floor is off by default (`Models.MinHitboxShare` = 0), because Megabonk's hitboxes are tall capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton) and fitting them undid OSRS proportions. `FitHitbox` now logs a `resize ...` line, and re-applies the elite/miniboss enlargement once Megabonk has made it. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Boss and elite size caps** | 0.1.13 (tier ceilings, `Models.BossMaxHeight`); 0.1.14 applies the caps after Megabonk's late enlargement. Quick tests passed. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **README in the release zip** | Checked: 0.1.0 to 0.1.11 shipped the first README (\"Megabonk's Forest map becomes Lumbridge\"); 0.1.12's zip has the current one. It still names `PlayerFit` (renamed `Models.AdventurerScale` in 0.1.12) and lacks `BossMaxHeight`, `Camera.Distance` (0.1.13), `MinHitboxShare` and `Minimap.Zoom` (0.1.15). Have `tools/package.py` refuse a README that doesn't mention the version's config keys. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Listing text: \"Lumbridge's map is in every OSRS install\"** | Only true after a first login. Not checked from the docs session (the listing text isn't visible here). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Real Giant Mole fight** | At the swamp's dark hole or in the Mole lair: its own arena, dig to a new spot, OSRS stats instead of Megabonk's boss. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Monster rosters per map from NPC spawn data** | Which monsters actually live in each map's area, from the offline data, instead of hand-picked `bonk_base_enemy` lists. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Hand-over playtest mode** | A test mode the creator plays by hand that still writes self-checks, so features autoplay can't reach get tested. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Per-feature Melty test checks** | e.g. `evolution`, `skilling-gathered`, `mole-dig`, `prayer-blocked`, `pathing-around-wall`, `casket-opened`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Colours paler than OSRS** | Under Megabonk's lighting and post-processing; textured faces are one average colour. Compare side by side with OSRS. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Autoplay hugging walls** | Autoplay's circle ignores walls; steer it with the pathing distance field. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **`hooks.json` behind the code** | Ten patches have no row, so the preflight can't catch a renamed target, and five rows have no patch ([Architecture](architecture.md#harmony-patches)). |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **HUD sprites in the `ui` sheet** | 0.1.17's HUD draws interface sprites by id from `UiSprite` (orbs, XP counter, chatbox, prayer glow, health bars, minimap frame 1177, compass 169) and the `q8_full` font, none of them `ui` rows, so the preflight doesn't check they exist in a player's cache. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Sheet statuses that don't match the code** | `ui.run_timer` says verified but isn't drawn; `hitsplat_poison` built but unused; `skills.unlocks` duplicates `weapons.gear_reqs`; drops' skilling `effect` strings aren't what runs. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Bonkscape's data edits on other maps** | Weapons, tomes, characters and remapped enemies keep their OSRS stats and names on Megabonk's other maps. Decide whether to restore them off Lumbridge. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **Skilling spots aren't marked** | Trees and rocks that are spots look like any other; the rock spot is a Tin rocks object but says copper. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Docs checks in the release steps** | `tools/package.py` runs `check_docs.py --head --release` (every check but the version one, whose changelog entry comes after the build and test) and refuses to build the zip on any FAIL (`--skip-docs` for emergencies, with a warning). The checker now also fails on a patch-table row with no patch in the code (the stale `EnemyHpBar.Set` case), and `docs_state.json` no longer counts as a changed source. The prose side is the `wiki-update` skill (`.claude/skills/wiki-update/`): run it after each version's build and test ([How to update these docs](updating-docs.md#the-docs-checker)). |\n\n## Done\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | The hub | One launcher for the tools: `Bonkscape Hub.cmd` or the Desktop shortcut starts `tools/hub` (port 8789), which starts the wiki and sketch servers and links them and the other docs. A static BSWiki export is prepared for hosting, not published ([The hub](hub.md)). |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | Playability pass | 0.1.12: pathing, roomier collision, bigger adventurer, prayer bar |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | Map sketch tool | `tools/sketch` with surface, underground and instance views |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | Full cache on this PC | The RuneLite cache replaced with the full archive (backup kept); preflight 143/143 phase-1 assets; `bonk worldscan` |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | The real Lumbridge | 0.1.7 to 0.1.11; passed the publish test |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | Phase 1 systems | 0.1.0 to 0.1.5; passed the publish test |\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/ sheets/ -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "gotchas", "text": "# Gotchas\n\nHard-won lessons, grouped by topic. Numbers in brackets are the numbered gotchas in `docs/MODLOG.md` (keep both in\nstep: MODLOG is the short log, this page explains). Unnumbered ones were found while writing the wiki.\n\n## Melty and the loader\n\n- **Melty must be started by the user, not from Claude's shell** [1]. `Start-Process melty://...` from the Claude\n  desktop app runs Melty inside the app's MSIX package; its AppData writes (the test file, `settings.properties`) land in\n  `Packages/Claude_*/LocalCache`, invisible to Megabonk, which Steam starts.\n- **Melty disables BepInEx between its own launches** [2] (renames `winhttp.dll` to `winhttp.dll.melty-off`). Iterate\n  with `test_release` runs rather than launching Megabonk directly.\n- **The BepInEx build Melty installs isn't the listed one.** The listing says 6.0.0-pre.2; the installed build is\n  **6.0.0-be.697** (.NET 6.0.7). Compile against `BepInEx/core` from the game folder (`lib/bepinex-melty`), not the\n  GitHub pre.2 zip.\n- **Interop assemblies only exist after a first Melty test launch** (`BepInEx/interop`). Without them the plugin builds\n  without its game code (`INTEROP` undefined), and you get a stub.\n- **`{game:custom-old-school-runescape}` is the Steam OSRS folder, which has no cache.** That's why the plugin searches\n  RuneLite's and the official client's cache folders itself.\n- **Self-checks are read line by line from the checks file**, verdict first: `pass osrs-cache` or `fail osrs-cache: why`.\n  `osrs-cache=pass` or a bare name aren't read. List in the recipe's `test.checks` only names the mod reports (0.1.0's\n  test failed with every check missing).\n- **A 1-run test is a quick check**; only a test of 2+ runs with every self-check passing in each run lets a new mashup\n  be published.\n\n## IL2CPP and Harmony\n\n- **Stripped Unity members** [3]. Members Megabonk never uses are missing, and calling them throws *\"Method unstripping\n  failed\"* (0.1.1's test failed on it). Missing: `AudioClip.Create/SetData` (all runtime clip creation),\n  `Renderer.forceRenderingOff`, `shadowCastingMode`, `receiveShadows`, `AudioSource.playOnAwake/spatialBlend`,\n  `ScreenCapture.CaptureScreenshot`. Present: `Mesh.vertices/colors32/triangles`, `Texture2D.LoadRawTextureData`,\n  `Renderer.enabled`, `GUI.DrawTexture`. Before relying on a member, scan the interop assemblies for\n  `throw new NotSupportedException(\"Method unstripping failed\")`.\n- **Rebuilt members crash natively** [19]. Some stripped members aren't missing: Il2CppInterop *rebuilds* them from\n  Unity's reference code, and a rebuilt copy can disagree with the game's Unity. `GUI.DrawTextureWithTexCoords` did:\n  it smashed the stack (coreclr `c0000005`) on the first HUD frame of every run, 0.1.17-0.1.21. A bound member has a\n  `NativeMethodInfoPtr_<name>` field in its interop type; a rebuilt one doesn't. `bonk unstripped <Bonkscape.dll>\n  <interopDir>` lists every rebuilt member the plugin calls, and `tools/package.py` refuses to package when there is\n  one not on its known-safe list. Draw part of a sprite from its own cut texture (`UnityConv.SpritePart`) instead.\n- **Sound without AudioClips** [4]: OSRS sounds are synthesised and mixed into the output from an injected\n  MonoBehaviour's `OnAudioFilterRead` on the AudioListener's object, re-attached when scenes replace the camera.\n- **Harmony on IL2CPP virtual methods recurses** [5]. Calling the original from a patch goes back through virtual\n  dispatch into the patch: stack overflow. Never let Harmony run the original of a virtual/override (`GetIcon`,\n  `GetDescription`). Set data fields instead (`WeaponData.icon`, `TomeData.description`), or reimplement and return\n  false (`GetName` reads `localizedName` itself).\n- **`ReadOnlySpan` overloads** [6] in interop (`AudioClip.SetData`, `Il2CppStructArray` constructors) break overload\n  resolution and reflection lookups. Cast sizes to `long`; avoid reflection over those methods.\n- **Name collisions** [11] with Megabonk's global types: `MeshData` (alias it inside the namespace), the `Assets`\n  namespace.\n- **Static initialisers that touch Unity can kill a whole class.** 0.1.0's test logged *\"The type initializer for\n  'Bonkscape.Core.UnityConv' threw an exception\"* on every use. Create Unity objects lazily, on the main thread.\n\n## Megabonk runtime\n\n- **Megabonk's transforms are scaled and rotated for its own art** [7]: enemy and player renderer bounds report about\n  4.5 m. OSRS models are separate objects that follow their owner (positioned every `LateUpdate`, facing the player or\n  the movement), not children of Megabonk's model.\n- **Level-up and shrine windows pause the game** [8] (`deltaTime` 0). Autoplay timers use unscaled time; press the\n  first `UpgradeButton.SelectUpgrade()`, and `BaseEncounterWindow.ChooseOffer(0)` for shrine windows.\n- **The player object appears a moment after the run starts** [9]: start-of-run setup keys off `MyPlayer.Instance`,\n  and a new player object means a new stage.\n- **The Forest stage's structure** [15]: 600 m square centred on (0, 10, 0), built from generated tile prefabs\n  (`ProceduralTileGeneration.tilesParent/newRoot/collider`) plus prop roots. Layers: Ground 8, Object 12, Water 4,\n  TransparentFX 1 (tree camera colliders), minimap 14. Camera collision is 1\\|8\\|12; spawns raycast Ground\\|Object\n  inside `SpawnPositions.minX..maxZ`, which `FindBounds` recomputes, so override it in a postfix. A catch box\n  `WorldCollider` sits at y -60 (top about -30). (Learned from the 0.1.6 diagnostic build.)\n- **Moving the player** [16]: `TeleportPlayerImmediate`/`TeleportPlayer` alone don't stick during the spawn intro.\n  Wait until `!isTeleporting && grounded`, then set `playerMovement.rb.position` (velocity 0) and the transform, and\n  repeat for a moment. (0.1.7 and 0.1.8 built the arena but never reported a kill, pickup, prayer or XP drop; 0.1.8\n  added this wait, and 0.1.9, with re-wound ground triangles, was the first arena build to pass.)\n- **Megabonk's bosses and minibosses** are recognised in `Content.ApplyEnemies` as `Miniboss*` names or\n  `maps == None && hp >= 1000`; their stats are left alone.\n\n## OSRS cache and models\n\n- **Players' caches are partial** (the client downloads models on demand), hence stand-ins and graceful fallbacks\n  everywhere. The creator's PC uses `OSRS.CacheFolder = D:/Modding/osrscache/cache`, a full cache, for testing; this\n  PC's RuneLite cache now has the full archive too (preflight: 143/143 phase-1 assets).\n- **OSRS NPC models need their standing frame** [12] or they T-pose. Lighting is computed before the pose and the NPC\n  scale after it, as the client does.\n- **Facing** [10]: MODLOG says OSRS models face +z after flipping OSRS y and z (yaw offset 0). Since `UnityConv` also\n  flips z (0.1.7, next point), they face -z (south) in Unity, so `EnemySkins` and `PlayerSkin` use a 180 degree\n  `YawOffset`.\n- **Handedness** [13]. OSRS axes (x east, y down, z north) are right-handed; Unity is left-handed. `MeshData` keeps\n  OSRS's frame with y and z flipped (a rotation), so `UnityConv` flips z once more (a reflection), or every model is\n  mirrored (the sword in the wrong hand, the River Lum west of the castle). A reflection reverses winding, so triangles\n  are re-wound: Unity mesh colliders and raycasts are one-sided, and ground facing down let the player and Megabonk's\n  spawn raycasts fall through (fixed in 0.1.9).\n- **The current map index (5) is unnamed** [14]: one group per region numbered `x << 8 | y`, file 0 terrain (16-bit\n  attributes, a trailing byte), file 1 objects, readable without XTEA keys. Older caches name them `m{x}_{y}`/`l{x}_{y}`.\n- **Textures are one average colour.** Faces with a texture are drawn in its sprite's average colour, part of why\n  Lumbridge looks paler than in OSRS.\n\n## Sizing and the arena\n\n- **Measure the character once, upright** [18]. Player collider bounds read 0 (or tilted) at some moments. Note that\n  `Sizing.Reset()` is never called, so the height is measured once per **game session**, not per run: switching to\n  an adventurer whose Megabonk character has a different collider keeps the first measurement.\n- **Arena colliders** [17]: walls are separate meshes in 8x8-tile cells, hidden while between camera and adventurer.\n  MODLOG describes the first version, colliders on layer 0. Since 0.1.11 they sit on a free physics layer (the highest\n  unnamed one) that is set to collide with the player's and the enemy layer, while Megabonk's camera, spawn raycasts\n  and projectiles ignore it.\n- **Monster hitboxes read 0 at spawn, then turn out huge.** `Enemy.collider` bounds are 0 when `InitEnemy` runs and\n  go live a moment later, which is also when Megabonk enlarges elites and minibosses; `FitHitbox` re-sizes then.\n  Megabonk's hitboxes are tall capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton), so \"never smaller than the hitbox\" made monsters\n  far too big: the floor is off by default since 0.1.15 (`Models.MinHitboxShare`).\n- **Megabonk's camera isn't always `Camera.main`.** The wall hiding looks for `PlayerCamera`'s own camera; the minimap\n  has a separate orthographic camera (whose `orthographicSize` `Minimap.Zoom` divides).\n- **`Bonk.Active` is per map, not per stage**: every stage of the Forest map gets the same Lumbridge.\n\n## Build, release and docs\n\n- **Renaming a config key is how you reset a default.** BepInEx keeps the value already in a player's `.cfg`, so a\n  new default never reaches existing installs. `HitboxFill` became `MinHitboxShare` in 0.1.15 for that reason (and\n  `PlayerFit` became `AdventurerScale` in 0.1.12, with a new default); the old lines are then ignored.\n- **Bump `Plugin.Version` for every upload**; the version Melty shows comes from the release, the log line from the DLL.\n- **The DLL records the commit it was built from**: its informational version is `1.0.0+<HEAD hash>`. Uncommitted\n  changes aren't reflected, so a zip built from a dirty tree carries the previous commit's hash (0.1.0 to 0.1.3 all\n  say `7b77aa6`).\n- **`tools/package.py` copies `README.md` as it is.** Update the README before packaging: 0.1.7 to 0.1.11 shipped the\n  pre-arena README describing \"Megabonk's Forest map becomes Lumbridge\".\n- **The preflight writes generated code even when it has phase-1 findings.** Check its exit code (4 = open items).\n- **`sheets/hooks.json` is behind the code**: ten patches have no row, five rows have no patch\n  ([Architecture](architecture.md#harmony-patches)). The preflight can only verify targets that have a row.\n- **Starting weapons are set in the `DataManager.Load` postfix**, once per game start; the character select panel\n  computes them live, so it can show a weapon the run doesn't give until Megabonk restarts (untested).\n\n<!-- sources: docs/MODLOG.md -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "hub", "text": "# The hub\n\nOne local page that links every Bonkscape web tool and starts, stops and restarts their servers, so nothing has to be\nstarted by hand. It runs on this PC only, at <http://localhost:8789>.\n\n## Starting it\n\n- **Desktop:** double-click **Bonkscape Hub**. It runs `pythonw`, so no console window opens. Make the shortcut once\n  with `python tools/hub/hub.py --shortcut` (or the button at the bottom of the hub).\n- **Repo:** double-click `Bonkscape Hub.cmd` in the repo root (a console flashes and closes).\n- **Terminal:** `python tools/hub/hub.py --open`.\n- **Claude Code:** the `bonkscape-hub` entry in `.claude/launch.json` (serves the hub without opening a browser).\n\nStarting the hub starts the wiki and the map sketch tool when they aren't running, then opens the hub in your browser.\nLaunching it again while it runs just opens the page. When `hub.py` changed since the running hub started, the new\nhub replaces it; the servers keep running. `python tools/hub/hub.py --stop-all` stops the hub and every server.\n\n## What's on it\n\n| Section | What | Port |\n|---|---|---|\n| BSWiki | `tools/wiki-site/server.py`: `docs/wiki` and `docs/dev`, with links to the player home, getting started, the dev home, changelog, docket, gotchas and this page | 8791 |\n| Map sketch tool | `tools/sketch/server.py`: the world map from your cache, your outlines and the Ideas layer, plus a link to the map ideas write-up | 8790 |\n| Docs | Markdown the wiki site doesn't show, rendered by the hub's own viewer (`doc.html`): the README, `docs/design/` (map ideas, UI style), `docs/MODLOG.md`, `docs/preflight.md`, and osrs-kit's README, `docs/`, `docs/research/` and `tools/music/README.md` | 8789 |\n| Folders | Opens the repo, `sketches/`, `dist/`, osrs-kit or the hub's logs in Explorer | |\n| Commands | The docs checker, table generator, map ideas build, packaging, the wiki export, the offline OSRS Wiki, the music lookup and `osrs.exe gamevals`, with absolute paths and a Copy button | |\n\nEach server card shows whether it's running, its port and pid, who started it (the hub, or something else such as\nClaude Code's preview) and since when, with Start, Stop, Restart and Log buttons. **Start all**, **Stop all** and\n**Quit** (leaving the servers running, or stopping them too) are at the top.\n\n## How it handles servers\n\n- **Reuse.** The hub recognises a server by what it serves (the wiki by `/api/nav`, the sketch tool by its `app.js`),\n  not just by a busy port, so a server started elsewhere (Claude Code's preview, a terminal) is reused, never doubled.\n- **Free ports.** When another program holds a server's port, Start takes the first free port from the default + 100\n  (8890, 8891, ... for the sketch tool) and remembers it; the card links there. The defaults stay 8789 to 8791.\n- **No windows.** Servers run under `python.exe` with no window (`CREATE_NO_WINDOW`), their output going to a log.\n  They keep running when the hub quits or crashes, and the next hub finds them.\n- **Older code.** When a running server's `server.py` changed after the server started, its card says so, and Restart\n  loads the new code. The hub never restarts a server by itself.\n- **Stop** ends the process that holds the port (found with `netstat -ano`), also one the hub didn't start; the page\n  asks first in that case.\n\n## Logs and state\n\nOutside the repo, in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\hub\\`:\n\n- `logs\\<server>.log`: each server's output (the card's Log button shows the end), trimmed past 1 MB.\n- `logs\\hub.log`: the hub's own output when it runs without a console.\n- `state.json`: the hub's port, and each server's last port and pid.\n- `hub.ico`: the shortcut's icon, drawn by `hub.py` (no image file in the repo).\n\nIf double-clicking does nothing, read `hub.log`, or run `python tools/hub/hub.py --open` in a terminal to see the error.\n\n## Safety\n\n- It listens on 127.0.0.1 only. It refuses requests whose `Host` isn't `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` (DNS rebinding), and\n  its buttons send an `X-Bonkscape-Hub` header that another website can't send to it, so no web page can start or stop\n  anything.\n- The doc viewer serves only the files `DOCS` in `hub.py` lists; the folder buttons open only `FOLDERS`.\n- Stdlib Python, nothing to install. Made for Windows: elsewhere pids come from `lsof`, and there's no shortcut and no\n  older-code check.\n\n## Adding a tool\n\nIn `tools/hub/hub.py`, add a row to `SERVICES` for a server (id, name, default port, script, a probe path and a\nfunction that recognises the answer, links), to `DOCS` for Markdown the hub should render, or to `COMMANDS` for a\ncommand to copy. A reload of the page shows it. Then add it to the table above and to\n[Architecture](architecture.md#projects).\n\n## Hosting BSWiki\n\nPrepared, **not done**: nothing is published, and there's no remote repo or site.\n\n`python tools/hub/export_wiki.py` writes BSWiki as a static site to `build/bswiki-site/` (gitignored): the wiki site's\n`index.html`, `app.js` and `style.css`, the Markdown pages, `api/nav` and `api/pages` (what the local server's API\nreturns), `robots.txt` and a `_headers` file asking search engines not to index it, and `.nojekyll` (so GitHub Pages\nserves the `.md` files as they are). It saves what the wiki server serves, so it's the local site page for page.\n`--with-dev` adds the developer pages; `--serve` shows the export on <http://localhost:8799>.\n\n**What would be public:** the player pages (`docs/wiki`) by default. With `--with-dev`, also the developer pages:\nthe architecture with every Harmony patch on Megabonk, the docket, gotchas, test history and changelog. Never map\ntiles, sprites, models, renders or anything else read from the OSRS cache or Megabonk: the export is text only and\nrefuses a page that embeds an image or any other file. Player pages link into the developer pages in a few places;\nthose links break when the developer pages are left out, and the export lists them.\n\nThe export uses relative paths, so it works at a domain's root or in a subfolder. Two ways to put it online:\n\n- **Cloudflare Pages:** `npx wrangler pages deploy build/bswiki-site --project-name bswiki`. To keep it private, put a\n  Cloudflare Access application (Zero Trust; free for up to 50 users) in front of the `pages.dev` hostname, allowing\n  only your e-mail address.\n- **GitHub Pages:** a small public repo holding only the export (say `bswiki`, served at\n  `https://<user>.github.io/bswiki/`), so Bonkscape's own repo can stay private. On a free account Pages needs a public\n  repo, and the site is public either way.\n\n<!-- sources: tools/hub/ -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "index", "text": "# BSWiki: developer pages\n\nHow Bonkscape is built, why it is the way it is, and what's next. Player-facing pages are in [BSWiki's player pages](../wiki/index.md).\nWritten against **0.1.20** (code at `782ce3f`).\n\n| Page | What it covers |\n|---|---|\n| [Architecture](architecture.md) | Projects, load sequence, the background asset build, sheets to code, the run lifecycle, the arena pipeline, every Harmony patch, tools, build and release |\n| [Sheets reference](sheets-reference.md) | Every sheet and column, what reads it, and what the preflight checks |\n| [Gotchas](gotchas.md) | Hard-won lessons from `MODLOG.md`, grouped by topic |\n| [Testing](testing.md) | Melty test mode, self-checks, footage review, the test history |\n| [Changelog and patch notes](changelog.md) | Every version 0.0.1 to 0.1.20: date, commit, test, patch notes and changes |\n| [Docket](docket.md) | Ideas and tasks by milestone, with status |\n| [How to update these docs](updating-docs.md) | What to update with every version, the table generator and the checker |\n| [The hub](hub.md) | One page that starts and links the wiki, the map sketch tool and the docs (`Bonkscape Hub.cmd`); hosting BSWiki |\n\n## Where things are\n\n```\nsheets/*.json                      design data (source of truth)\nsrc/Bonkscape.Cache/               OSRS cache reader (no Unity)\nsrc/Bonkscape.Plugin/              the BepInEx plugin\n  Core/                            runner, asset build, sizing, Unity conversion, rows, JSON\n  Systems/                         one file per system\n  Patches/CorePatches.cs           leaderboards, data load, death screen\n  Generated/Sheets.g.cs            generated from the sheets, don't edit\nsrc/Bonkscape.Tools/               bonk.exe (preflight, codegen, cache and map tools)\ntools/package.py                   release zip\ntools/sketch/                      map sketch tool (port 8790)\ntools/wiki-site/                   this wiki's site (port 8791), table generator, docs checker\ntools/hub/                         the hub (port 8789): starts and links the tools; Bonkscape Hub.cmd launches it\ndocs/MODLOG.md                     short log: versions, workflow, numbered gotchas\ndocs/preflight.md                  generated preflight report\ndocs/wiki/, docs/dev/              these wikis\n```\n\n## The working loop\n\n1. Change the sheets (design) or the code.\n2. `bonk preflight ...` until phase 1 has 0 open items (regenerates `Sheets.g.cs` and `cache_assets.json`).\n3. Bump `Plugin.Version`, `dotnet build -c Release`, `python tools/package.py <version>`.\n4. Upload and test through Melty; read the self-checks and review the footage ([Testing](testing.md)).\n5. Update the docs: changelog and patch notes, affected wiki pages, docket, statuses\n   ([How to update these docs](updating-docs.md)).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "sheets-reference", "text": "# Sheets reference\n\n`sheets/*.json` is the design data and the source of truth. Every system starts as rows here; the code reads them\nthrough `Generated/Sheets.g.cs`. Each file has the same shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"sheet\": \"prayers\",\n  \"about\": \"One line on what a row is\",\n  \"columns\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"...\", \"phase\", \"status\"],\n  \"rows\": [ { \"id\": \"protect_melee\", \"name\": \"Protect from Melee\", \"...\": \"...\", \"phase\": 1, \"status\": \"verified\" } ]\n}\n```\n\n<!-- gen:sheet-list -->\n| Sheet | Rows | Columns | Row statuses |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `audio.json` | 17 | 6 | 14 built, 3 todo |\n| `bosses.json` | 2 | 9 | 1 built, 1 todo |\n| `cache_assets.json` | 177 | 9 | 5 todo, 172 verified |\n| `characters.json` | 5 | 17 | 2 built, 2 todo, 1 verified |\n| `drops.json` | 12 | 10 | 7 built, 3 todo, 2 verified |\n| `enemies.json` | 11 | 20 | 1 built, 4 todo, 6 verified |\n| `evolutions.json` | 4 | 10 | 2 built, 2 todo |\n| `hooks.json` | 26 | 9 | 6 built, 20 verified |\n| `maps.json` | 5 | 17 | 4 todo, 1 verified |\n| `passives.json` | 11 | 10 | 9 built, 2 todo |\n| `prayers.json` | 3 | 12 | 3 verified |\n| `skills.json` | 10 | 8 | 5 built, 5 verified |\n| `ui.json` | 16 | 8 | 4 built, 12 verified |\n| `waves.json` | 7 | 8 | 7 built |\n| `weapons.json` | 13 | 22 | 7 built, 5 todo, 1 verified |\n<!-- /gen:sheet-list -->\n\n## Rules the preflight checks on every sheet\n\n`bonk preflight` (`src/Bonkscape.Tools/Preflight.cs`) loads every sheet except `cache_assets.json` and checks:\n\n- **Every row has every column**, and no row has a column the sheet doesn't declare.\n- **No cell is unfilled**: `null`, `\"\"` and `\"todo-value\"` are findings. Use `\"none\"` or `[]` for \"nothing\".\n- **`status`** is `todo`, `built` or `verified`.\n- **`phase`** sorts the findings: phase-1 findings are \"open items\" and make the preflight exit with code 4; phase 2/3\n  findings are listed as \"unfinished by design\". The report and the generated code are written either way, so read\n  the exit code.\n- **References** to other sheets resolve (`'goblin' is not a row of enemies`), with `none`/`any` allowed where noted.\n- **Megabonk names** resolve against `Assembly-CSharp.dll` in the interop folder: enum values (`EWeapon`, `ETome`,\n  `EEnemy`, `ECharacter`, `EMap`, `EStat`, `EStatModifyType`; a `new:` prefix skips the check), and for `hooks`, classes\n  and methods.\n- **OSRS ids** resolve in the dev cache: definitions decode and their models load (NPCs, items, objects, kits, worn\n  items, spot animations), sprites and fonts exist, sounds synthesise to something. Each asset becomes a row of\n  `cache_assets.json`, also checked against this PC's own (player) cache.\n\nThe report goes to `docs/preflight.md`, `cache_assets.json` is rewritten, and the generated rows go to\n`Generated/Sheets.g.cs` when a `genOut` path is given (pass `-` to skip).\n\n### Status, by convention\n\n| Status | Means |\n|---|---|\n| `todo` | Designed, not built. The plugin ignores rows with `phase` > 1 whatever their status. |\n| `built` | In the code. |\n| `verified` | Seen working in a Melty test run (self-check or footage). |\n\nThe preflight only checks the spelling; keeping statuses honest is a manual step at each release\n([How to update these docs](updating-docs.md)).\n\n## characters\n\nOne row per playable adventurer; each takes over a Megabonk character. Read by `Content.ApplyCharacter`,\n`Osrs.BuildPlayer`, `PlayerSkin`, `Combat.CurrentCharacter`, `TestMode` (first row = autoplay's adventurer).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | Row key. | |\n| `name` | Shown name (character select, `GetName`). | |\n| `style` | `melee` / `ranged` / `magic`. Decides which skill the default damage trains and which weapons can be its starting weapon. | |\n| `attack_style` | `accurate` / `aggressive` / `defensive`: melee XP goes to Attack / Strength / Defence. | |\n| `starting_weapon` | Weapon row it starts with before skill upgrades. | row of `weapons` |\n| `bonk_base_character` | Megabonk `ECharacter` whose slot, prefab, movement and hitbox it takes. | `ECharacter` value |\n| `hp`, `armor`, `damage`, `area`, `cooldown`, `speed`, `luck` | Stat modifiers replacing the Megabonk character's own for `MaxHealth`, `Armor`, `DamageMultiplier`, `SizeMultiplier`, `AttackSpeed` (flat) and `MoveSpeedMultiplier` (addition), `Luck` (flat). 0 = remove Megabonk's. | |\n| `osrs_player_model` | JSON: `osrs_items` (worn item ids), `osrs_kits_male` (identity kit ids), `osrs_colors` (0 = kit colours, the only value used), `osrs_stand_anim` (sequence for the pose). | every kit and worn item resolves; the whole body builds |\n| `unlock_condition` | `always`, or a condition for phase-2 characters (`defence_1_attack_60`, `total_level_250`). Not read by the code yet. | |\n| `phase`, `status` | See above. | |\n\n## weapons\n\nOne row per OSRS weapon; each reuses a Megabonk weapon's behaviour. Read by `Content.ApplyWeapon`, `Combat`,\n`Content.StartingWeapon`, `Osrs` (items, sprites, sounds).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `name` | Key and shown name. | |\n| `style` | `melee` / `ranged` / `magic`: which skill its damage trains, and which adventurers can start with it. | |\n| `bonk_base` | Megabonk `EWeapon` it takes over, or `new:...` for a weapon type that doesn't exist yet. | `EWeapon` value |\n| `damage`, `cooldown`, `area`, `amount`, `speed`, `pierce`, `duration`, `knockback` | Replace `WeaponData.damage`, `endCooldown`, `projectiles`, `projectileSpeed`, `projectileBounces` (from `pierce`), `attackDuration`, `knockback`, and the `baseStats` entries `DamageMultiplier`, `SizeMultiplier` (area), `Projectiles`, `ProjectileSpeedMultiplier`, `ProjectileBounces`, `DurationMultiplier`, `KnockbackMultiplier`. | |\n| `level_curve` | List of `Stat:Type:Value` that replaces the weapon's upgrade pool. | each `EStat` and `EStatModifyType` |\n| `gear_reqs` | `\"starting_weapon\"`, or `{\"skill\": level}`: levels needed to **start** a run with it. | skills are rows of `skills` |\n| `osrs_item_id` | Item for the icon (and model). | item resolves |\n| `osrs_icon_sprite_id` | Sprite to use as the icon instead (spells), or `none`. | sprite resolves |\n| `osrs_projectile_or_spotanim_id` | `item:<id>`, `spotanim:<id>` or `none`. **Not used by the plugin yet.** | resolves |\n| `sfx_id` | Attack sound. Decoded, **not played yet**. | sound synthesises |\n| `spec_name`, `spec_effect` | Special attack name and effect. **Not built.** | |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## evolutions\n\nA max-level weapon plus a gear passive becomes its upgrade when a casket opens. Read by `Systems/Evolutions.cs`.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | Key. | |\n| `from_weapon` | Weapon row, or `any`. | row of `weapons` or `any` |\n| `required_passive` | Passive row that must be held (any level). | row of `passives` |\n| `max_weapon_level` | Weapon level needed (8). | |\n| `result_name` | New name. | |\n| `result_stats` | `{\"EStat\": multiplier}` applied to the weapon's `baseStats` (restored at the next run). | `EStat` names |\n| `osrs_item_id`, `osrs_icon_sprite_id` | New icon. | resolve |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## passives\n\nOSRS gear, one item per slot; each takes over a Megabonk tome. Read by `Content.ApplyTome` and the `GetAvailableTomes`\npostfix.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `name` | Key and shown name. | |\n| `bonk_base_tome` | Megabonk `ETome` it takes over. Tomes with no row leave Lumbridge's offers. | `ETome` value |\n| `bonk_stat` | `Stat:Type` of the tome's stat modifier. | `EStat`, `EStatModifyType` |\n| `value_per_level` | Modifier value. | |\n| `max_level` | Level cap: no longer offered at this level. | |\n| `gear_slot` | Holding one item of a slot removes the others of that slot from the offers. | |\n| `osrs_item_id` | Icon. | item resolves |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## enemies\n\nOne row per OSRS monster; each takes over Megabonk enemies. Read by `Content.ApplyEnemies`, `Osrs.BuildEnemy`,\n`EnemySkins`, `Prayer`, `Bosses`.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `name` | Key and shown name. | |\n| `osrs_npc_id` | NPC whose definition gives the model, recolours and stand animation. | NPC builds |\n| `osrs_npc_alternates` | Stand-in NPCs, tried in order when the first isn't in the player's cache. | each builds |\n| `combat_level` | OSRS combat level. Not used yet. | |\n| `style` | `melee` / `ranged` / `magic`: what protection prayer blocks it, and its style icon. | must be one of the three |\n| `bonk_base_enemy` | Megabonk `EEnemy` values it takes over. `Miniboss*` and boss bases keep Megabonk's stats. | `EEnemy` values |\n| `hp`, `damage`, `speed`, `knockback_resist` | Replace the base's `EnemyData` values (not for minibosses and bosses). | |\n| `xp_value` | Not used yet (XP comes from damage). | |\n| `drop_table_id` | Not used yet (drops are global). | row of `drops` (`table_id`) |\n| `model_ids`, `recolors` | `from_npc_def` (the only value): taken from the NPC definition. | |\n| `scale` | Size multiplier on top of OSRS proportions. | |\n| `animation_ids` | JSON plan for animations (`walk`, `dig`, `attack`, with a `phase`). Not used yet: the 0.2.0 milestone (animations). | |\n| `maps` | Map rows it belongs to. | rows of `maps` |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## bosses\n\nBoss behaviour layered on an enemies row. Read by `Systems/Bosses.cs` (phase 1: the Mole's dig pattern and threshold).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | Key, referenced by `maps.boss_id`. | |\n| `enemy_id` | The enemies row. | row of `enemies` |\n| `attacks` | JSON list: `name`, `style`, `telegraph_ms`, `damage`, `pattern`. Only `burrow_teleport_every_<N>s` is read (dig period and telegraph). | each `style` is melee/ranged/magic |\n| `phase_thresholds` | HP fractions; the first one speeds up the dig (x0.66 period). | |\n| `music_override` | Not used yet. | |\n| `pet_item_id`, `pet_rate` | Pet item and 1-in-N rate. Not used yet. | item resolves |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## maps\n\nOne row per map. Read by `Bonk`, `Arena`, `Osrs.BuildArena`, `Skilling`, `MapProps`, `Content`.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `name` | Key and shown name (`GetName` on the map). | |\n| `bonk_base_map` | Megabonk `EMap` it takes over; `Bonk.Active` is true on this map. | `EMap` value |\n| `bonk_base_stage` | Stage index whose timeline `waves` edits (and that autoplay starts). | |\n| `osrs_area` | `[x0, y0, x1, y1]` in OSRS world tiles, built as the arena; `[]` for none. | x0 < x1, y0 < y1; the area builds from the dev and player caches with no missing region |\n| `spawn_tile`, `boss_tile` | `[x, y]` for the adventurer and the boss portal. | inside the area, a walkable tile within 3 |\n| `osrs_music_track` | Track name. Music isn't built. | track exists (reported phase 2+) |\n| `props` | `{\"tree\"|\"oak\"|\"rock\"|\"bush\": [object ids]}` for the Forest fallback. | objects resolve |\n| `skilling_nodes` | List of `{type, osrs_object_id | osrs_npc_id, count, respawn_s}`. `count` is used by the Forest fallback; `respawn_s` by both. | object or NPC resolves |\n| `waves_id` | Its `waves` rows (by `map_id`). | row of `waves` |\n| `boss_id` | `bosses` row or `none`. | row of `bosses` or `none` |\n| `fallback_enemy` | Enemy row used when a Megabonk enemy has no row, or a monster's model is missing. | row of `enemies` |\n| `length_minutes`, `special_rule` | Planned (`skull` for the Wilderness). Not used yet. | |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## waves\n\nSpawn plan per map; Megabonk's own credit system paces spawns. Read by `Content.ApplyEnemies`.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `map_id` | Map row (also the sheet's key column, so preflight shows rows by map). | row of `maps` |\n| `minute` | When the row applies. | |\n| `enemy_ids` | Enemy rows. | rows of `enemies` |\n| `spawn_rate`, `max_alive` | `megabonk` (keep Megabonk's pacing). Not read. | |\n| `events` | `start`: the stage timeline's start enemies. `unlock`: the rows' non-miniboss bases get `canSpawnAfterTime = minute x 60`. `swarm`: the `ESwarm` event at that minute spawns these. `miniboss`, `boss`: documentation of Megabonk's own events (not read). | |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## drops\n\nWhat things drop and what picking them up does. Read by `Rows` (food, potion, coins, casket) and `Loot`.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `table_id` | `lumbridge_common`, `skilling`, `giant_mole`. Not used to pick drops yet (drops are global). | |\n| `item` | Item name, used in chat lines. | |\n| `kind` | `coins`, `food`, `potion`, `casket`, `rare`, `pet`. `Rows` picks food (with `bonk_base_pickup` Health), the potion, coins and the casket by kind. | |\n| `bonk_base_pickup` | Megabonk pickup it reskins (`Gold`, `Health`, `Chest`) or `new`. | |\n| `weight_or_rate` | Weight among food rows, or a per-kill chance (potion 0.025), or `megabonk`. | |\n| `amount` | Not read. | |\n| `osrs_item_id` | Model and icon. | item resolves |\n| `effect` | `heal:N` is read for food; the potion's `prayer:7+0.25` matches the code but is hard-coded; skilling effects aren't read (the code uses Megabonk's Haste/Shield). | |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## prayers\n\nProtection prayers, in key order. Read by `Prayer`, `Hud`, `Osrs` (sprites, sounds).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `name` | Key and name. | |\n| `style_blocked` | Enemy style it blocks. | |\n| `block_normal`, `block_boss` | Share of damage removed (1.0 / 0.5). | |\n| `drain_per_sec` | Points per second while on. | |\n| `key` | Default key as a `KeyCode` name. The code's defaults come from `Prayer.Keys` config; keep them the same. | |\n| `osrs_prayer_sprite_id` | Prayer book icon (prayer bar). | sprite resolves |\n| `osrs_overhead_sprite_id` | `group:frame` overhead icon. | sprite resolves |\n| `sfx_id` | Sound when turned on. | sound synthesises |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## skills\n\nPersistent skills. Read by `Skills`, `Hud`, `CharacterSelect`, `Prayer`, `Skilling`.\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `name` | Key (also the `skills.json` key) and name. | |\n| `trained_by` | Documentation of what trains it; the logic is in `Skills.SkillFor`, `Prayer.Tick`, `Skilling.Gather`. | |\n| `xp_rate` | XP per point of damage, per second praying, or per gather. **Read by the code.** | |\n| `osrs_skill_icon_id` | Skill icon sprite (also the style icons for attack/ranged/magic). | sprite resolves |\n| `unlocks` | `{\"level\": weapon}`. Documentation: the code uses `weapons.gear_reqs`. Keep both in step. | weapons are rows |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## ui\n\nOSRS presentation elements. Read by `Hud`, `Osrs` (sprites, fonts), `CorePatches` (death text).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | Key the code looks up (`hitsplat_damage`, `chat_line`, `death_screen`, `missing_cache`...). | |\n| `element` | Kind of element. | |\n| `osrs_sprite_or_font_id` | Sprite group (number), `font:<name>` or `item:<id>`. | resolves |\n| `text` | Text template; `chat_line`, `death_screen` and `missing_cache` texts are used as written. | |\n| `position`, `billboard` | Documentation; positions are in `Hud.cs`. | |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## audio\n\nSounds and music. Read by `Rows.Sfx` (sound ids by row id) and `Osrs` (which sounds to synthesise).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | Key the code looks up (`player_hit`, `level_up`, `prayer_off`...). | |\n| `event` | Documentation. | |\n| `osrs_sound_or_track_id` | `sfx:<id>`, `track:<name>` or `jingle:<name>`. | sound synthesises; tracks and jingles reported as needing the synthesiser |\n| `fallback` | `sfx:<id>` used when the main one isn't a sound, `megabonk` or `none`. | sound synthesises |\n| `phase`, `status` | | |\n\n## hooks\n\nEvery place Bonkscape touches Megabonk. Documentation checked by the preflight; the code doesn't read it.\n**It's behind the code**: see the [patch list](architecture.md#harmony-patches).\n\n| Column | Meaning | Preflight |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | Key. | |\n| `system` | Which system. | |\n| `bonk_assembly` | Assembly (`Assembly-CSharp`). | |\n| `class_or_table` | Megabonk class. | the class exists |\n| `method_or_row` | Method, or field for `data row`. | the method (or field/getter) exists |\n| `patch_kind` | `prefix`, `postfix`, `poll`, `call (...)`, `data row`. | |\n| `purpose` | What it does. | |\n| `rows_it_serves` | Sheet rows it serves (`weapons.*`, `ui.hitsplat_*`) or `-`. | the sheets exist |\n| `status` | | |\n\n## cache_assets (generated)\n\nWritten by the preflight; don't edit. One row per OSRS asset the other sheets use.\n\n| Column | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `osrs_id` | `kind:id`, e.g. `npc:3031`, `area:lumbridge`. |\n| `kind` | `npc`, `item`, `worn`, `kit`, `object`, `spotanim`, `sprite`, `font`, `sound`, `track`, `player`, `area`. |\n| `decoded_by` | Decoder chain. |\n| `converted_to` | `mesh`, `icon`, `texture`, `font`, `clip`... |\n| `used_by` | `sheet.row.column` references. |\n| `render_settings` | Icon settings note. |\n| `player_cache` | Present in this PC's own OSRS cache. |\n| `detail` | Name and size, or why it failed. |\n| `status` | `verified` (decodes from the dev cache) or `todo`. |\n\n<!-- sources: sheets/ src/Bonkscape.Tools/Preflight.cs src/Bonkscape.Tools/Codegen.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Rows.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "testing", "text": "# Testing\n\nBonkscape is tested through **Melty's test runs**: Melty installs a release on this PC, starts Megabonk (through\nSteam) with a test file in place, records the window, collects the mod's self-checks, and the run is reviewed from\nits footage. Melty must be started by the user ([Gotchas](gotchas.md#melty-and-the-loader)).\n\n## Test mode (`Systems/TestMode.cs`)\n\n**Turning on.** At load, and every 3 seconds afterwards until it's found, the mod looks for\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Melty\\test\\bonkscape.json`. Its fields:\n\n| Field | Use |\n|---|---|\n| `checks` | Path of the checks file the mod appends to (`bonkscape-checks.txt` in the same folder). Test mode is on when it's set. |\n| `seed` | Seeds autoplay and run randomness (chest/shrine placement, skilling). Default 1. |\n| `run` | Run number, logged. |\n\nIf the file turns up after some checks already passed, they're written out again. `Dev.AutoStartRun = true` turns on\nthe same autoplay without Melty (checks are then only logged).\n\n**Autoplay.**\n\n1. **Main menu**: once the cache is decoded and Megabonk's data loaded, wait 3 s, select the first adventurer\n   (Warrior) and start the Lumbridge map's stage 0 directly (`MapController.StartNewMap`).\n2. **Level-ups**: every 0.8 s of real time (the game is paused), press the first active `UpgradeButton`; if none but\n   Megabonk is levelling up, `UpgradePicker.AutoSelectUpgrade`; otherwise take the first offer of any open reward\n   window (shrines). In a chest window (0.1.16): press Open, then Take about 3 s later; discard the item if the window\n   is still open after 8 s.\n3. **Prayer**: every 4 s, switch to the protection prayer against the style most monsters within 10 m use.\n4. **Movement** (`PlayerInput.MovementInput` postfix): a slow circle (0.35 rad/s), bent away from any monster within\n   7 m, turned into camera-relative input.\n5. **Potions**: after 3 kills, if no potion has been drunk and none is on the ground, the next kill always drops one,\n   so `osrs-item-picked` and the potion path get exercised. Only the first potion is boosted (0.1.6 onwards), so the\n   chat isn't flooded.\n6. **Death**: 6 s on the death screen, then `DeathScreen.Restart()` and a new run.\n\n## Self-checks\n\nEach is reported once per game session as a `pass <name>` line (or `fail <name>: why`) in the checks file, and as\n`check passed: <name>` in the log. The recipe's `test.checks` lists the same seven names.\n\n| Check | Passes when | Code |\n|---|---|---|\n| `osrs-cache` | The cache decoded and the OSRS icons were applied to Megabonk's data. Fails at load when no cache is found. | `Runner.Update`, `Plugin.Load` |\n| `run-started` | A Lumbridge run has been active for 1 s. | `TestMode.Tick` |\n| `lumbridge-arena` | The real Lumbridge was built and the adventurer moved in. (Added in 0.1.7.) | `Arena.Build` |\n| `osrs-enemy-killed` | A monster wearing an OSRS model died. | `Combat` (`EnemyDied`) |\n| `osrs-item-picked` | Coins, food, flying coins or a prayer potion were picked up. | `Loot` |\n| `prayer-switched` | A protection prayer was turned on. | `Prayer.Toggle` |\n| `xp-drop` | An XP drop was shown during a run. | `Hud.Init` (XP drop event) |\n\n## What Melty checks\n\nBesides the self-checks, every run is checked for: `installed` (the right version), `started`, `loaded` (BepInEx\nloaded `Bonkscape.dll`), `no-crash`, `responding`, `picture` (the window shows something), `ran-to-end` (3 or 4\nminutes), `stray-loaders`, and **`loader-errors`**: any warning or error logged from the mod's files fails the run.\nSo a `LogWarning` in a normal code path is a test failure; keep warnings for real problems.\n\n## Footage review\n\nMelty records frames of the window (for example 91 frames over a 3-minute run, laid out in contact sheets). A reviewer\n(a Claude Code session using Melty's `test_review`) looks through them and records a verdict with evidence: the\ntimestamp, frame and what was seen (\"00:48: 'Protected!' over the adventurer as an OSRS guard's hit is blocked\"), and\na summary. A run **counts** only when Melty's checks, the self-checks and the footage review all pass.\n\n- A **1-run test** is a quick check.\n- A **test of 2+ runs**, each counting, is what lets a new mashup be published (the \"publish test\"). 0.1.5 and 0.1.11\n  passed it.\n\nWhat footage review is good for: things self-checks can't see. That the adventurer is in the courtyard, that\nmonsters reach you around walls, that the prayer bar and \"Protected!\" show, that sizes look right. What it misses:\nanything autoplay doesn't do (other adventurers, most weapons, skilling on purpose). Since 0.1.16 autoplay opens\nchests, so caskets get exercised; an evolution still needs a maxed weapon and its gear passive by chance.\n\n## Test history\n\nTimes are local (UTC-5). From Melty's release list and test results.\n\n| Version | Test | Runs | Result | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.0.1 | `69badf81` | | passed | Stub: loader and cache discovery |\n| 0.1.0 | `f950c212` | 1 x 4 min | **failed** | `UnityConv` type initializer threw; no self-check reported |\n| 0.1.1 | `3d4554e1` | 1 x 3 min | **failed** | \"Method unstripping failed\" errors; `osrs-item-picked` and `prayer-switched` missing |\n| 0.1.2 | `212af9d8` | | passed | |\n| 0.1.3 | `a5e4376c` | | passed | |\n| 0.1.4 | `196b766b` | | passed | |\n| 0.1.5 | `00b12845` | 2 x 4 min | **passed (publish test)** | All six self-checks, footage reviewed |\n| 0.1.6 | `4038aeb7` | 1 x 3 min | failed (expected) | Diagnostic build; its probe check `probe-enemies-on-slab` never reported. The six normal checks passed. |\n| 0.1.7 | `6c2d57ed` | 1 x 3 min | **failed** | Arena built; kill, pickup, prayer and XP checks missing |\n| 0.1.8 | `f9b58412` | 1 x 3 min | **failed** | Same four missing |\n| 0.1.9 | `531bf1f4` | | passed | First arena build to pass |\n| 0.1.10 | `ce9989f6` | | passed | |\n| 0.1.11 | `09ad9949` | 2 x 4 min | **passed (publish test)** | All seven self-checks; footage: courtyard start, castle, river and bridges, swamp, cow and Giant Frog minibosses, death and restart |\n| 0.1.12 | `3e8c9d4c` | 1 x 3 min | passed (quick check) | Prayer bar, \"Protected!\", monsters around walls. Review: adventurer still read small (log: adventurer 4.80 m, guard 4.47 m), which led to 0.1.13 |\n| 0.1.13 | `2f85d870` | 1 x 4 min | passed (quick check) | All seven self-checks |\n| 0.1.14 | `77b7beb2` | | passed (quick check) | |\n| 0.1.15 | `13a522b9` | | passed (quick check) | |\n| 0.1.16 | `9e1854a7` | | passed (quick check) | Autoplay opens chests |\n| 0.1.17 | `aebf6011` | 1 x 4 min | **failed** | Megabonk crashed in `coreclr.dll` (c0000005) at 0:18, before a run started; only `osrs-cache` reported. The window couldn't be recorded. |\n| 0.1.18 | `b09071b7` | 1 x 4 min | **failed** | Same crash in `coreclr.dll` at 0:17 without the `EnemyHpBar.Set` patch; only `osrs-cache` reported |\n| 0.1.18 | `48b6a423` | 1 x 4 min | **failed** | The same crash again, at 0:16; only `osrs-cache` reported |\n| 0.1.19 | `9f22aab1` | 1 x 3 min | passed (quick check) | No crash; all seven self-checks. Run with `Debug.OsrsHud=false` (per the main session). |\n| 0.1.20 | `9634e18a` | | running | Run with `Debug.HideMegabonkHud=false` (per the main session) |\n\nBlank cells weren't looked up. `mcp__melty__test_result` with the test id gives the full record.\n\n## Testing locally\n\n- `Dev.AutoStartRun = true` plays a Lumbridge run by itself on your own launches. Remember Melty switches BepInEx off\n  between its launches.\n- The log (`BepInEx/LogOutput.log`) has the useful lines: `OSRS assets ready in ... ms`, `Lumbridge built from the\n  OSRS cache in ...`, `Lumbridge arena: ...`, `sizing: ...`, `skin <enemy> (<tier>) as <name>: ...`, `check passed:`,\n  and every chat line as `[chat]`.\n- Offline: `bonk preflight` checks the sheets against the interop assemblies and both caches; `bonk worldscan`\n  checks every map region decodes; `bonk render` and `bonk world` make images to look at.\n\nGaps (per-feature checks, a hand-over playtest mode, the other adventurers) are on the [docket](docket.md).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/TestMode.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "dev", "slug": "updating-docs", "text": "# How to update these docs\n\nThe `wiki-update` skill (`.claude/skills/wiki-update/`) runs this whole process, safely while other sessions commit\nto the same folder: start there after each version is built and its Melty test has a result.\n\n**The changelog and the wiki get updated with every version.** A version isn't finished until its changelog entry,\npatch notes and the wiki pages it touches say what the code now does. The wikis describe the code as it is, not the\nplan: a planned feature is marked planned until it's built.\n\n## With every version\n\n1. **Changelog** ([changelog.md](changelog.md)): add the version at the top with\n   - the build date and time (local, UTC-5), the commit it was built from and the commit that holds its code,\n   - the Melty test id and result (update it when the test finishes or its footage is reviewed),\n   - **patch notes**: 1 to 4 short, player-facing bullets (paste these into the Melty release changelog),\n   - **changes**: what changed for developers, naming files, settings and sheet columns.\n2. **Wiki pages**: run the checker (below) and re-read every page it lists as touched by the changes. Fix what's no\n   longer true. New settings go on [Settings](../wiki/settings.md), new patches in\n   [Architecture](architecture.md#harmony-patches), new gotchas in [Gotchas](gotchas.md) and `docs/MODLOG.md`.\n3. **Version lines**: the version and code commit at the top of [the wiki home](../wiki/index.md) and\n   [the dev home](index.md), and `documented_commit` in `tools/wiki-site/docs_state.json`.\n4. **Statuses**: rows that were seen working in a Melty test become `verified` in their sheet; rows newly built become\n   `built`. Then regenerate the tables.\n5. **Docket** ([docket.md](docket.md)): move finished tasks to done, add what the test or review turned up.\n6. **Tables**: `python tools/wiki-site/gen_tables.py`.\n7. **Check**: `python tools/wiki-site/check_docs.py` must pass. `tools/package.py` won't build a release until\n   `--head --release` passes ([below](#the-docs-checker)).\n\n## Generated tables\n\nTables of sheet data (weapons, monsters, gear, prayers, skills, waves, drops, UI and audio rows, hooks, the sheet list)\nare generated from `sheets/*.json`. In a page they sit between markers:\n\n```markdown\n<!-- gen:weapons -->\n(generated: don't edit by hand)\n<!-- /gen:weapons -->\n```\n\n`python tools/wiki-site/gen_tables.py` rewrites every marked table; `--check` only reports stale ones. To add a table,\nwrite a `t_<name>()` function in `gen_tables.py`, add it to `TABLES`, and put the markers in a page. Names come from\n`sheets/cache_assets.json`, so run the preflight first when OSRS ids changed.\n\n## The docs checker\n\n`python tools/wiki-site/check_docs.py` checks what can be checked mechanically, against the working tree. With\n`--at REV` it reads the code (`src/Bonkscape.Plugin`) from commit REV instead, which ignores other sessions'\nunfinished edits in the same folder and any code committed after REV; docs pages and sheets still come from the\nworking tree. Use `--at <code commit>` when you document a released version (the commit that set its\n`Plugin.Version`), `--head` (the same as `--at HEAD`) for the latest commit, and the plain run to check uncommitted\nwork.\n\n**It gates every release:** `python tools/package.py <version>` runs `check_docs.py --head --release` first and\nrefuses to build the zip (non-zero exit, nothing written to `dist/`) when any check fails. `--release` leaves out the\nVersion check, because a version's changelog entry and wiki-home line are written after its build and Melty test (the\n`wiki-update` skill); every other check applies, so the session that adds a setting, patch, sheet column or self-check\ndocuments it in the same commit. Fix the FAIL lines and package again. `package.py --skip-docs` builds anyway, for\nemergencies only; it prints a warning, and the docs still need fixing.\n\n| Check | Fails when |\n|---|---|\n| Tables | A generated table is out of date. |\n| Settings | A `Config.Bind` key in `Plugin.cs` isn't on the Settings page. |\n| Patches | A `[HarmonyPatch]` target has no row in Architecture's patch table, or a row in that table (its first column, `(args)` ignored) has no patch in the code. |\n| Sheet columns | A sheet column isn't mentioned in the Sheets reference. |\n| Self-checks | A name in `TestMode.Checks` isn't on the Testing page. |\n| Version | `Plugin.Version` has no changelog heading, or the wiki home doesn't name it. Skipped with `--release`. |\n| Links | A relative link points to a missing page or heading. |\n\nIt also lists **pages to re-read**: every page ends with a `<!-- sources: ... -->` comment naming the code and sheets\nit describes. The checker compares those against the files changed since `documented_commit` (in\n`tools/wiki-site/docs_state.json`, which itself doesn't count) plus uncommitted changes; with `--at REV` or `--head`,\nonly the files changed from `documented_commit` to REV. A listed page isn't necessarily wrong; it's where to look.\nAfter re-reading them, set `documented_commit` to the commit you checked against.\n\nWhat it can't check: whether the prose is true. That takes reading the code (or a test run) for each listed page.\nThings only a run can show (whether Megabonk counts minibosses as bosses, how big things look) stay marked\nunconfirmed until a Melty run, its footage or a log line shows them.\n\n## Writing style\n\n- Say what the code does, with the numbers it uses. Quote in-game text exactly, in italics.\n- Mark anything planned with its phase (the generated tables do this from `status`).\n- Player pages (`docs/wiki`) explain how to play; developer detail (file names, hooks) goes in `docs/dev`.\n- Link pages with relative links (`[Prayer](prayer.md#prayer-points)`); the site and GitHub both follow them.\n\n## The site\n\n`python tools/wiki-site/server.py 8791`, then open <http://localhost:8791>. It renders `docs/wiki` and `docs/dev`\nstraight from disk, so a refresh shows your edits. The `bonkscape-wiki` entry in `.claude/launch.json` starts it from\nClaude Code's preview. Simplest: double-click `Bonkscape Hub.cmd` (or the Desktop shortcut), which starts the site and\nlinks its pages ([The hub](hub.md)).\n\n<!-- sources: tools/wiki-site/ -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "adventurers", "text": "# Adventurers\n\nYou play an OSRS adventurer in place of a Megabonk character. Each adventurer takes over one Megabonk character's\nslot: its place on character select, its movement and its hitbox. Bonkscape changes its name, stats, starting weapon,\nportrait and model.\n\n<!-- gen:characters -->\n| Adventurer | Style (attack style) | Starting weapon | Megabonk slot | Stat changes | Worn OSRS items | Unlock | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Warrior** | melee (aggressive) | Dragon scimitar | SirOofie | max HP +50, armour +0.15, move speed -0.02 | Rune full helm, Rune platebody, Rune platelegs, Dragon scimitar | always | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Ranger** | ranged (accurate) | Magic shortbow | Robinette | armour +0.05, move speed +0.075 | Green d'hide body, Green d'hide chaps, Magic shortbow | always | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Mage** | magic (accurate) | Fire Strike | Fox | move speed +0.04, luck +0.15 | Blue wizard hat, Blue wizard robe, Staff of fire | always | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Pure** | melee (aggressive) | Dragon scimitar | Ninja | max HP -40, damage +0.35, move speed +0.1 | Dragon scimitar | defence 1 attack 60 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Ironman** | melee (defensive) | Dragon scimitar | SirChadwell | max HP +30, armour +0.1, luck +0.25 | Ironman helm, Ironman platebody, Ironman platelegs | total level 250 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:characters -->\n\nStat changes are Megabonk stat modifiers. For each stat in the row (max HP, armour, damage, size, attack speed, move\nspeed, luck), Bonkscape removes the Megabonk character's own modifier for that stat and adds the row's value, if it\nisn't zero. Move speed is added to Megabonk's move speed multiplier; the others are flat. Everything else about the\nMegabonk character is left as Megabonk made it.\n\nPure and Ironman are planned: they're in the sheet with unlock conditions, but **not built**, so character select\nshows Megabonk's own `Ninja` and `SirChadwell` characters in their slots.\n\n## Starting weapons\n\nEach adventurer starts with its row's weapon. Once your [skills](skills-and-xp.md) are high enough, it starts with a\nstronger weapon of the same style instead: the one with the highest skill requirement you meet.\n\n| Adventurer | Default | Upgrades |\n|---|---|---|\n| Warrior (melee) | Dragon scimitar | 70 Attack: **Abyssal whip** |\n| Ranger (ranged) | Magic shortbow | 55 Ranged: **Red chinchompa**; 75 Ranged: **Toxic blowpipe** |\n| Mage (magic) | Fire Strike | 75 Magic: **Trident of the seas**; 94 Magic: **Ice Barrage** |\n\nThese requirements only decide the weapon you **start** with. Level-ups offer all eight weapons whatever your levels\n([Weapons](weapons-and-evolutions.md)).\n\nThe character select panel shows which weapon the selected adventurer will start with. Bonkscape sets the starting\nweapon when Megabonk loads its data, which happens as the game starts. From the code, a level gained during a play\nsession shows on the panel right away but may only reach the run after you restart Megabonk. That hasn't been tested\nyet ([docket](../dev/docket.md)).\n\n> **Warrior and Attack.** The Warrior fights in the *aggressive* style, so its melee damage trains **Strength**, not\n> Attack ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md#what-trains-what)). Attack is trained by melee damage from an *accurate*\n> adventurer, which means the Ranger or Mage using a melee weapon picked up on level-up.\n\n## Looks\n\nEach adventurer is built from OSRS player parts in your cache: the male identity kits listed in the sheet (head, jaw,\ntorso, arms, hands, legs, feet) plus the worn items above, which hide the parts they cover, in the kits' own colours.\nThe model stands in the first frame of OSRS's standing animation (808). It isn't animated yet: no walking, attacking\nor dying moves ([Known limitations](known-limitations.md)).\n\nThe model follows your character, feet on the ground, and turns to face the way you move. Megabonk's own character\nmodel is hidden. Character select portraits are rendered from the same OSRS model.\n\nIf a worn item isn't in your cache, the adventurer is built without it. If the body can't be built at all, you see\nMegabonk's character.\n\n## Size\n\nMegabonk's character height is measured once per game session, the first time it stands upright. Your adventurer is drawn at\nthat height times **`Models.AdventurerScale`** (default **1.6**, from 0.5 to 3). Lumbridge is scaled to match, so the\nworld keeps OSRS proportions around you.\n\nYour **hitbox** is still Megabonk's: a bigger adventurer doesn't get hit more.\n\nMonsters are drawn on your adventurer's scale: an OSRS human stands about as tall as your adventurer, and goblins,\nrats and chickens keep their OSRS ratios to them ([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#size)).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/PlayerSkin.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/CharacterSelect.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Sizing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Osrs.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs sheets/characters.json sheets/weapons.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "gear-passives", "text": "# Gear passives\n\nMegabonk's *tomes* (the passive upgrades offered on level-up) become OSRS gear. Each piece of gear takes over one\nMegabonk tome: its place in the level-up offers, its level cap and the one stat it raises. Bonkscape sets the stat,\nthe amount per level and the cap from the row, gives it the OSRS name and an icon rendered from your cache, and writes\nits description, for example *\"Amulet of fury (neck slot): +8% damage per level, up to level 8.\"*\n\n<!-- gen:passives -->\n| Gear | Slot | Megabonk tome | Stat | Per level | Max level | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Amulet of fury** | neck | Damage | damage (multiplication) | +8% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Berserker ring** | ring | Precision | crit chance (flat) | +7% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Barrows gloves** | hands | Cooldown | attack speed (addition) | +7.5% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Rune platebody** | body | Armor | armour (flat) | +12% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Boots of lightness** | feet | Agility | move speed (addition) | +15% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ring of wealth** | ring | Luck | luck (flat) | +8% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Amulet of glory** | neck | Golden | coins gained (addition) | +12% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Kraken tentacle** | weapon upgrade | Size | attack size (addition) | +10% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Tome of fire** | shield | Duration | duration (addition) | +15% | 8 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Godsword shard** | weapon upgrade2 | Knockback | knockback (addition) | +20% | 3 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Fire cape** | cape | Health | max HP (flat) | +25 | 8 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:passives -->\n\n## One item per gear slot\n\nLike your OSRS equipment, each slot holds one item. Once you've picked a piece of gear, the other pieces for the same\nslot stop appearing in level-up offers:\n\n- **Neck**: Amulet of fury *or* Amulet of glory.\n- **Ring**: Berserker ring *or* Ring of wealth.\n- Every other slot has a single item.\n\nA piece also stops being offered once it reaches its max level (8).\n\n## What's left out\n\nIn Lumbridge, level-ups offer only the gear above. Megabonk tomes without a row (Health and Knockback, for example,\nuntil the Fire cape and Godsword shard are built) don't appear there.\n\nTwo pieces matter for [evolutions](weapons-and-evolutions.md#evolutions): the **Kraken tentacle** (Abyssal whip into\nAbyssal tentacle) and the **Tome of fire** (Fire Strike into Fire Surge).\n\nThe Fire cape and Godsword shard are planned (phase 2), along with their evolutions, the Infernal cape and the\nArmadyl godsword (i).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs sheets/passives.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "getting-started", "text": "# Getting started\n\n## What you need\n\n- **Megabonk** on Steam.\n- **Old School RuneScape**, logged in at least once on this PC with RuneLite or the official client, so its game\n  files (the *cache*) exist. Bonkscape reads models, map data, icons, fonts and sounds from that cache and never writes\n  to it.\n- **Melty**, which installs the mod and its loader (BepInEx 6 for IL2CPP games) by itself.\n\n> **Your cache fills up as you play OSRS.** The OSRS client downloads most game files the first time it needs them.\n> If you've only logged in once, some monsters or items may be missing from your cache. Bonkscape then uses an OSRS\n> stand-in that *is* in your cache (another chicken for a chicken, for example; see\n> [Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#stand-ins)). If Lumbridge's map regions are missing, you get Megabonk's Forest\n> with OSRS scenery instead of the real Lumbridge ([Maps](maps.md#when-lumbridge-isnt-built)).\n\n## Installing\n\nBonkscape is installed through Melty. It isn't public yet, so for now that means a test build from the creator.\n\nMelty puts BepInEx in Megabonk's folder and the mod in `BepInEx/plugins/Bonkscape/`. That folder holds:\n\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `Bonkscape.dll` | The mod |\n| `Bonkscape.Cache.dll` | The OSRS cache reader |\n| `README.md`, `LICENSE`, `LICENSES/RuneLite-cache-BSD-2-Clause.txt` | Readme and licences |\n\nNo OSRS or Megabonk files are in the download.\n\n## Where Bonkscape looks for your OSRS files\n\nIt checks these folders in order and uses the first that holds a cache:\n\n1. The `OSRS.CacheFolder` setting ([Settings](settings.md)). When that's empty, the `OSRS_CACHE` line in\n   `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\settings.properties`, if there is one.\n2. The OSRS folder Melty passes in (the `OSRS_DIR` line in that same file), then `jagexcache\\oldschool\\LIVE` inside it.\n3. RuneLite's cache: `%USERPROFILE%\\.runelite\\jagexcache\\oldschool\\LIVE`.\n4. The official client's cache: `%USERPROFILE%\\jagexcache\\oldschool\\LIVE`.\n5. `%ProgramData%\\Jagex\\oldschool`.\n\nEvery file is opened read-only and shared, so OSRS can stay open while you play.\n\nIf none has a cache, the screen says *\"Bonkscape can't find Old School RuneScape's game files. Run OSRS once, then\nstart Megabonk again.\"* and the mod stays out of the way.\n\n## First launch\n\n1. Start Megabonk the way Melty tells you to. The first start after installing takes longer, because BepInEx\n   prepares itself.\n2. While the main menu loads, Bonkscape decodes what it needs from your cache in the background: monsters, the three\n   adventurers, items and icons, sprites, fonts, sounds, then the Lumbridge arena. Menus work meanwhile; the log line\n   `OSRS assets ready in ... ms` says how long it took.\n3. On character select, a **Bonkscape** panel on the right shows your combat level, your skill levels and the weapon\n   the selected adventurer will start with ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#character-select-panel)).\n4. Pick **Warrior** (it takes Megabonk's `SirOofie` slot), **Ranger** (`Robinette`) or **Mage** (`Fox`) and start a\n   run on Megabonk's Forest map, which Bonkscape renames **Lumbridge & Swamp**. Bonkscape weapons, gear and adventurers count\n   as unlocked whatever your Megabonk progress is.\n5. After Megabonk's spawn intro you're moved into the castle courtyard. A chat line greets you: *\"Welcome to\n   Lumbridge. Press 1, 2 or 3 to pray against melee, missiles or magic.\"*\n\nOnly the Forest map becomes Lumbridge. Megabonk's other maps aren't fully plain Megabonk, though: Bonkscape edits\nMegabonk's data once when the game loads, so the weapons, tomes and characters it reskins keep their OSRS names,\nicons and stats on every map, and the Megabonk enemies it remaps keep the OSRS rows' HP, damage and speed. On those\nmaps, monsters keep Megabonk's models and level-ups offer Megabonk's full pool\n([Known limitations](known-limitations.md)).\n\n## Leaderboards\n\nRuns with Bonkscape loaded never upload scores to Megabonk's Steam leaderboards.\n\n## Where your progress lives\n\n- Skills: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\skills.json` ([Skills and XP](skills-and-xp.md#saving)).\n- Settings: `BepInEx/config/gg.melty.bonkscape.cfg` in Megabonk's folder ([Settings](settings.md)).\n- Log: `BepInEx/LogOutput.log`. Bonkscape's lines start with `[Info   : Bonkscape]`, and every chat message is\n  logged too, as `[chat] ...`.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Cache/OsrsCache.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Patches/CorePatches.cs tools/package.py -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "glossary", "text": "# Glossary\n\n## Old School RuneScape\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **OSRS** | Old School RuneScape, Jagex's MMO. Bonkscape reads its game files from your PC. |\n| **Cache** | The folder of game files the OSRS client keeps (`main_file_cache.dat2` and `.idx` files). It fills up as you play, because the client downloads things the first time it needs them. |\n| **Gielinor** | The OSRS world. |\n| **Tile** | One square of the OSRS map. Positions like (3222, 3218) are OSRS world tiles: x east, y north. |\n| **Region** | A 64 x 64-tile block of the map, the unit the cache stores map data in. |\n| **NPC** | A non-player character, including every monster. Each has a numbered definition in the cache. |\n| **Identity kit** | One of the body parts (head, torso, legs...) a player model is built from. |\n| **Combat style** | Melee, ranged or magic. |\n| **Attack style** | How a melee attack trains: accurate (Attack), aggressive (Strength) or defensive (Defence). |\n| **Protection prayer** | A prayer that blocks one combat style: Protect from Melee, Missiles or Magic. |\n| **Hitsplat** | The small marker with a damage number over whoever was hit. Red for damage, blue for 0. |\n| **XP drop** | The `+XP` that floats up the screen when you gain experience. |\n| **Game tick** | OSRS's 0.6-second heartbeat. Bonkscape groups XP drops per tick. |\n| **Combat level** | One number summing up your combat skills, worked out with OSRS's formula. |\n| **Casket** | An OSRS reward container. In Bonkscape, Megabonk's chests. |\n| **Stand animation** | The looping idle animation of a model. Bonkscape uses its first frame as a static pose. |\n| **Spot animation (spotanim)** | A graphic effect such as a spell's projectile or impact. Named in the sheets, not used yet. |\n\n## Megabonk\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Run** | One game from character select until you die or win. |\n| **Stage** | One part of a map's run; the Forest map has several. |\n| **Tome** | Megabonk's passive upgrades. Bonkscape turns them into OSRS gear. |\n| **Level-up offer** | The choice of upgrades Megabonk shows when you level up. |\n| **Elite / miniboss / boss** | Bigger, stronger enemies. Megabonk enlarges them; Bonkscape caps how much of that it passes on. |\n| **Boss portal** | The object you use to call a stage's boss. |\n| **Shrine** | A Megabonk interactable that offers a reward. |\n| **Swarm** | A timeline event that spawns a crowd of one kind of enemy. |\n| **Hitbox** | The invisible shape that decides whether something hits. Bonkscape never changes hitboxes, only how things look. |\n\n## Bonkscape\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Adventurer** | Your OSRS character: Warrior, Ranger or Mage. |\n| **Arena** | The real Lumbridge, built from your cache, that replaces the Forest's ground. |\n| **Forest fallback** | Megabonk's Forest dressed in OSRS scenery, used when Lumbridge can't be built. |\n| **Gear passive** | A piece of OSRS gear that replaces a Megabonk tome. One per gear slot. |\n| **Evolution** | A maxed weapon plus its gear passive becoming its OSRS upgrade when a casket opens. |\n| **Stand-in** | Another OSRS NPC used when a monster's own model isn't in your cache. |\n| **Style icon** | The Attack, Ranged or Magic icon over a monster, showing its combat style. |\n| **Sheet** | One of the design data files in `sheets/*.json`. Every weapon, monster, prayer and so on is a row. |\n| **Phase** | Which milestone a row belongs to. Phase 1 is in the mod now; phases 2 and 3 are later. |\n| **Status** | A row's state: *todo* (planned), *built* (in the mod) or *verified* (confirmed in a Melty test run). |\n| **Preflight** | The `bonk preflight` tool that checks every sheet against Megabonk and an OSRS cache before a build. |\n| **Melty** | The service that installs, tests and publishes the mod. |\n| **Test mode / autoplay** | How Melty's automated test plays a Lumbridge run by itself. |\n| **Self-check** | A named result the mod reports to Melty during a test run, such as `prayer-switched`. |\n\n<!-- sources: sheets/ -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "hud-and-chat", "text": "# HUD and chat\n\nBonkscape draws an OSRS HUD over Megabonk's, laid out like OSRS's own interfaces and drawn with OSRS's sprites and\nfonts, read from your cache. In a Lumbridge run it hides the Megabonk pieces it replaces: the health bar (on the HUD\nand under your adventurer), the XP bar (its *LVL n* text stays) and the monsters' health bars. They come back when the\nrun ends, so Megabonk's other maps keep their own HUD. Megabonk's timer, kill counter and minimap stay (the minimap\nshows Lumbridge's OSRS map). Everything scales with the screen height in whole steps of 540 px: 1x at 720p, 2x at\n1080p, 3x at 1440p, 4x at 4K. Above 720p the chat box is one step smaller.\n\n*(unconfirmed: this HUD hasn't been seen in a Melty run yet; see [Known limitations](known-limitations.md).)* The\n`Debug.OsrsHud` setting turns it off, and with `Debug.HideMegabonkHud` off Megabonk's own bars stay up beside it\n([Settings](settings.md)).\n\n## In a run\n\n| Element | Where | What it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Minimap orbs** | Left of Megabonk's minimap, as in OSRS | From the top: the XP button, the **hitpoints** orb (your Megabonk HP), the **prayer** orb (your prayer points; lit while a prayer is on) and, when your character has an active ability, a **special attack** orb showing how far it has recharged, in %. Each orb drains from the top; its number is green when full, yellow at half and red when empty. |\n| **XP counter** | Left of the orbs | Your total XP over all skills, and under it a green strip: Megabonk's progress to its next run level. |\n| **XP drops** | Rising from under the XP counter into it | The skill icon and the amount, for about 2 s, grouped per 0.6 s tick ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md#xp-drops-and-level-ups)). Drops from the same tick line up under each other. |\n| **Health bars** | Over a monster's head, and over yours | OSRS's green-over-red bar. A monster's shows for 6 s after you hit it: 30 px wide, 50 for minibosses, 80 for bosses. Yours shows whenever you're below full health, and for 6 s after any hit. |\n| **Style icons** | Over the 10 nearest monsters, above their health bar | The Attack, Ranged or Magic skill icon for the monster's combat style ([Prayer](prayer.md)) |\n| **Hitsplats** | On a monster you hit (a little below its head), and on you when you're hit | OSRS's red hitsplat with the damage, or the blue one for 0. Each lasts 1.2 s. A monster shows two at most; further hits add their damage into one of them. Megabonk's own floating damage numbers (yours and the monsters') are hidden in Lumbridge. |\n| **Prayer panel** | Bottom right | The three protection prayers on a stone panel with their keys ([Prayer](prayer.md#the-prayer-panel)) |\n| **Overhead prayer** | Above your adventurer's health bar | The OSRS overhead icon of the active protection prayer |\n| **\"Protected!\"** | Above your adventurer | Flashes for 0.7 s when a prayer stops or halves a hit |\n| **Minimap frame and compass** | Round Megabonk's minimap | OSRS's minimap frame, with the compass in its socket turning as the camera turns. Drawn only when Bonkscape could measure where Megabonk's minimap is on screen. *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage, both that the minimap gets measured and that the compass points the right way)* |\n| **Coins** | Left side, about a third down | The OSRS coin stack for your amount, the amount in OSRS's colours (yellow, then white with K from 100,000, green with M from 10 million) and \"Coins\". Megabonk's own gold number and icon are hidden. |\n| **Chat box** | Bottom left corner | See [below](#chat-box) |\n| **Level-up** | Chat box, and at your feet | OSRS's level-up dialogue covers the chat box for 3 s: *\"Congratulations, you just advanced a Strength level.\"*, *\"Your Strength level is now 41.\"* and *\"Click here to continue\"*, with the skill's icon. OSRS's level-up fireworks play at your adventurer's feet, and keep playing while Megabonk's level-up window pauses the game. |\n| **Evolution** | Chat box | The new weapon's name, like *\"Fire Surge!\"*, as a dialogue for 3.5 s |\n| **Death message** | Centre | *\"Oh dear, you are dead!\"* in large red OSRS text. Megabonk's death screen title says it too. |\n| **Hint** | Above the prayer panel, first 45 s | *\"Pray against the icon over a monster: 1 Melee 2 Missiles 3 Magic\"* |\n\nBonkscape doesn't draw a run clock: Megabonk's own timer stays.\n\n## Chat box\n\nOSRS's chat box, cut down: it shows your last **4** lines, and only for 8 seconds after something new is said, then\nhides. It sits in the bottom left corner, only as tall as its lines. A level-up or evolution dialogue covers it while\nit shows. The same message twice in a row becomes one line with a count, like *\"You get some logs. (x3)\"*.\n\nWhat it says:\n\n| When | Message |\n|---|---|\n| A run starts | *Welcome to Lumbridge. Press 1, 2 or 3 to pray against melee, missiles or magic.* |\n| A skill levels up | *Congratulations, you just advanced a Mining level. You are now level 12.* |\n| You eat | *You eat the lobster. It heals some health.* |\n| You drink a prayer potion | *You drink some of your prayer potion.* |\n| Prayer runs out | *You have run out of Prayer points, you can recharge at an altar.* |\n| You pray with no points | *You need to recharge your Prayer at an altar.* |\n| A weapon evolves | *Your Fire Strike has become a Fire Surge!* |\n| The Giant Mole digs | *The Giant Mole burrows into the ground!* |\n| You gather | *You get some logs.* / *You manage to mine some copper.* / *You catch some shrimps.* |\n\nEvery chat line is also written to the BepInEx log as `[chat] ...`.\n\n## Character select panel\n\nOn character select, a **Bonkscape** panel on the right, on OSRS's stone background, shows:\n\n- your **combat level**, as *\"Combat Lvl: 3\"* ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md#combat-level)),\n- every skill in two columns, with its icon and level,\n- *\"Warrior starts with: Dragon scimitar\"*, the weapon the selected adventurer will start with\n  ([Adventurers](adventurers.md#starting-weapons)).\n\n## When your cache can't be found\n\nIf Bonkscape finds no OSRS cache, or decoding it fails, the screen shows *\"Bonkscape can't find Old School\nRuneScape's game files. Run OSRS once, then start Megabonk again.\"*\n\n## Sounds\n\nOSRS sound effects are synthesised from your cache's instrument data and mixed into Megabonk's audio, at\n`Audio.OsrsVolume` ([Settings](settings.md)). These play now: getting hit (and the different sound for a 0), level-ups\nand evolutions, each prayer going on, prayer off, running out of prayer, picking up coins, eating and drinking,\nchopping, mining and fishing.\n\nIn the sheet but **not played yet**: a sound for hitting monsters and for kills, and each weapon's own attack sound.\nMegabonk's own sounds play for those. OSRS **music and jingles** (Lumbridge's *Harmony*, the level-up jingle, the death\njingle) need an OSRS music synthesiser that isn't built, so Megabonk's music plays.\n\n<!-- gen:audio -->\n| Row | Event | OSRS sound or track | Fallback | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `enemy_hit` | hit | `sfx:2498` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `player_hit` | hit | `sfx:510` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `player_zero` | hit | `sfx:511` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `kill` | kill | `sfx:2498` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `pickup_item` | pickup | `sfx:2582` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `pickup_coins` | pickup | `sfx:3924` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `level_up` | level_up | `sfx:3925` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `level_up_jingle` | level_up | `jingle:level_up` | sfx:3925 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| `prayer_on_melee` | prayer_on | `sfx:2676` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `prayer_on_missiles` | prayer_on | `sfx:2677` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `prayer_on_magic` | prayer_on | `sfx:2675` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `prayer_off` | prayer_off | `sfx:2663` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `prayer_empty` | prayer_off | `sfx:2672` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `chop` | pickup | `sfx:2735` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `mine` | pickup | `sfx:3220` | none | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `death` | death | `jingle:dead` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| `lumbridge_music` | map_music | `track:Harmony` | megabonk | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:audio -->\n\n## UI rows\n\nThe OSRS sprites and fonts each element uses (`sheets/ui.json`):\n\n<!-- gen:ui -->\n| Row | Element | OSRS sprite / font | Text | Position | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `hitsplat_damage` | hitsplat | `1359` | {damage} | over_target | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `hitsplat_zero` | hitsplat | `1358` | 0 | over_target | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `hitsplat_poison` | hitsplat | `1360` | {damage} | over_target | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `hitsplat_font` | hitsplat | `font:p11_full` | digits | over_target | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `xp_drop` | xp_drop | `font:p11_full` | +{xp} | top_right | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `chat_line` | chat_line | `font:p12_full` | Congratulations, you just advanced a {skill} level. | bottom_left | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `chat_box` | chat_line | `1017` | none | bottom_left | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `death_screen` | death_screen | `font:b12_full` | Oh dear, you are dead! | center | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| `coin_stack` | coin_stack | `item:995` | {gp} | hud_gold | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `overhead_icon` | overhead_icon | `440` | none | over_player | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `style_marker_melee` | style_marker | `197` | none | over_enemy | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `style_marker_ranged` | style_marker | `200` | none | over_enemy | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `style_marker_magic` | style_marker | `202` | none | over_enemy | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `run_timer` | run_timer | `font:p12_full` | {mm}:{ss} | hud_timer | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `prayer_orb` | overhead_icon | `font:p11_full` | Prayer {points} | hud_prayer | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| `missing_cache` | chat_line | `font:p12_full` | Bonkscape can't find Old School RuneScape's game files. Run OSRS once, then start Megabonk again. | center | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:ui -->\n\nTwo rows aren't drawn although the sheet marks them done: `run_timer` (Bonkscape's OSRS-font clock was removed in\n0.1.7) and `hitsplat_poison` (nothing poisons yet).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/HudLayout.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/OsrsUi.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/MegabonkHud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/LevelUpFx.cs src/Bonkscape.Cache/SpotAnimFrames.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Chat.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Evolutions.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/CharacterSelect.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Loot.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Sfx.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/OsrsAudio.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Patches/CorePatches.cs sheets/ui.json sheets/audio.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "index", "text": "# BSWiki\n\nBonkscape is a Megabonk mod that puts an Old School RuneScape adventurer into a Megabonk horde-survival run through\nthe real Lumbridge. The town, monsters, items, icons, fonts and sound effects are read from your own OSRS install while\nthe game starts. Nothing from either game ships with the mod.\n\nThis wiki says how each system works **in the code as it is now**. It doesn't describe plans as if they were built.\n\n> **Version:** BSWiki matches Bonkscape **0.1.20** (code at `782ce3f`). What changed in each version:\n> [patch notes](../dev/changelog.md). How each version tested: [test history](../dev/testing.md#test-history).\n\n## Pages\n\n| Page | What it covers |\n|---|---|\n| [Getting started](getting-started.md) | What you need, installing through Melty, the first launch |\n| [Maps](maps.md) | The Lumbridge arena: what's built from your cache, spawn, boss portal, minimap, see-through walls |\n| [Adventurers](adventurers.md) | Warrior, Ranger and Mage: starting weapons, stats, looks and size |\n| [Weapons and evolutions](weapons-and-evolutions.md) | Every weapon, its Megabonk behaviour and level-ups; caskets and the two evolutions |\n| [Gear passives](gear-passives.md) | The OSRS gear that replaces Megabonk's tomes, one item per slot |\n| [Monsters and bosses](monsters-and-bosses.md) | Who spawns when, combat styles, sizes, the Giant Mole's dig |\n| [Prayer](prayer.md) | Protection prayers: keys, drain, how much they block, potions, the prayer bar |\n| [Skills and XP](skills-and-xp.md) | OSRS's XP table, what trains what, saving, unlocks by level, combat level |\n| [HUD and chat](hud-and-chat.md) | Hitsplats, XP drops, chat box, coins, banners, the character select panel |\n| [Skilling](skilling.md) | Trees, rocks and fishing spots, and what they give |\n| [Settings](settings.md) | Every config key, its default and what it does |\n| [Known limitations](known-limitations.md) | What isn't there yet, or behaves oddly |\n| [Glossary](glossary.md) | OSRS, Megabonk and Bonkscape terms |\n\n## Status labels\n\nEvery system comes from a row in the design sheets (`sheets/*.json`), and every row has a status. The wiki shows it\nthe same way everywhere:\n\n- <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span>: built and confirmed working in a Melty test run (self-checks or footage).\n- <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span>: in the mod, not yet confirmed in a test run.\n- <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span>: designed in the sheets but **not built**. Phase 2 and 3 are later\n  milestones; phase 1 is what's in the mod now.\n\n## In one minute\n\n- You start a run on Megabonk's first map. With Bonkscape loaded it's **Lumbridge & Swamp**: you appear in the\n  castle courtyard, and the castle, the River Lum, the church, the fields and the swamp are built from your cache.\n- You play one of three adventurers: [Warrior, Ranger or Mage](adventurers.md). Level-ups offer\n  [OSRS weapons](weapons-and-evolutions.md) and [OSRS gear](gear-passives.md) in place of Megabonk's.\n- [Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md) are chickens, goblins, giant rats, guards, cows and giant frogs, and the Giant\n  Mole is the boss. Each one fights in melee, ranged or magic, shown by the icon over its head.\n- Press **1 / 2 / 3** to [pray](prayer.md) against melee, missiles or magic.\n- Damage trains your OSRS [skills](skills-and-xp.md), and they're kept between runs. High levels change your starting\n  weapon.\n- Stand next to Lumbridge's trees, rocks and fishing spots to [skill](skilling.md) for coins, buffs and food.\n\nDeveloper documentation (architecture, sheets, gotchas, testing, changelog, task docket) is in [BSWiki's developer pages](../dev/index.md).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "known-limitations", "text": "# Known limitations\n\nWhat isn't there yet, or behaves differently from what you'd expect. The [docket](../dev/docket.md) tracks the work.\n\n## Not built yet\n\n- **Animations.** Your adventurer and every monster stand in their OSRS standing pose: no walking, attacking or dying\n  animations. They're the next milestone, 0.2.0.\n- **Music.** Megabonk's music plays. OSRS music and jingles (Lumbridge's *Harmony*, level-up, death) need an OSRS music\n  synthesiser.\n- **Special attacks.** Named in the weapons sheet, not built.\n- **OSRS projectiles and weapon sounds.** Weapons look and sound like their Megabonk base. Hitting and killing\n  monsters plays Megabonk's sounds, not OSRS's.\n- **Prayer altars.** The chat tells you to recharge at an altar, but there's none; prayer potions are the only refill.\n- **More adventurers, weapons, gear, monsters and maps.** Pure, Ironman, the Dwarf multicannon, Dharok's greataxe, the\n  Scythe of vitur, the Armadyl godsword, Dragon claws, the Fire cape, Godsword shards, Barrows, the Wilderness, God\n  Wars Dungeon and the Fight Caves are designed (phase 2 and 3) but not in the game.\n- **Pets, clue scrolls, the Mole's own drops** (Mole claw, Baby mole). Planned.\n\n## Works, with caveats\n\n- **Your cache decides what you see.** The OSRS client downloads models on demand. Monsters missing from your cache use\n  stand-ins; if Lumbridge's map regions are missing, you get the Forest instead.\n- **Megabonk's other maps change a little too.** Bonkscape edits Megabonk's data when the game loads, so its reskinned\n  weapons, tomes and characters keep their OSRS names, icons and stats on every map, and the Megabonk enemies it remaps\n  keep the OSRS rows' HP, damage and speed.\n- **Every Forest stage is the same Lumbridge.** The later stages are renamed *Lumbridge Swamp* and *Lumbridge Swamp\n  Caves* but build the same arena.\n- **Minibosses and the Giant Mole use Megabonk's stats** and Megabonk's own attacks; only ordinary monsters take the\n  sheet's HP, damage and speed.\n- **Defence can't be trained**: no phase-1 adventurer fights defensively. The Warrior trains Strength, not Attack.\n- **Starting weapon upgrades** are set when Megabonk loads; a level reached mid-session may only take effect after a\n  restart (not yet tested).\n- **Projectiles go through Lumbridge's walls**, yours and the monsters', because walls are only solid to bodies.\n- **Colours look paler than in OSRS** under Megabonk's lighting, and textured surfaces use one average colour.\n- **Hitboxes are Megabonk's.** Megabonk's enemy hitboxes are tall capsules, often taller than the OSRS model drawn\n  for them, so a hit can land a little outside a monster's shape.\n- **Megabonk's minibosses and boss portal** come from the Forest's own timeline and placement rules; Bonkscape only\n  moves them.\n- **Trees and rocks that are skilling spots** aren't marked.\n- **The OSRS HUD hasn't been confirmed in a run yet** (orbs, XP counter, health bars, prayer panel, level-up dialogue\n  and fireworks, minimap frame and compass). Unconfirmed until a Melty run's footage shows them: whether Megabonk's minimap gets measured (the frame and compass are drawn only then), which way the compass\n  turns, and how the layout sits next to what's left of Megabonk's HUD at each resolution.\n\n## Melty test runs\n\nThese only show up in Melty's automated test runs (autoplay):\n\n- The autoplay route often presses the adventurer and camera against walls in recordings.\n- Autoplay always plays the Warrior and always takes the first level-up offer, so the other adventurers and most\n  weapons aren't exercised by tests yet. (Since 0.1.16 it does open chests.)\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/ sheets/ -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "maps", "text": "# Maps\n\nBonkscape has one map so far: **Lumbridge & Swamp**, which takes over Megabonk's Forest map.\n<span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> (Melty publish test of 0.1.11: courtyard start, castle, river and\nbridges, swamp, minibosses, death and restart).\n\n## The Lumbridge arena\n\nThe arena is the real Lumbridge, built from **your own OSRS cache**: OSRS world tiles **(3140, 3140) to (3266, 3300)**,\n127 x 161 tiles across 16 map regions. That takes in the castle and its courtyard, the River Lum and its bridges, the\nchurch, the houses, the fields and Lumbridge Swamp, with about 11,800 placed OSRS objects.\n\nWhat's built:\n\n- **Terrain**: tile heights, colours and lighting like the OSRS client draws them, shaped overlay tiles (paths,\n  floors, shorelines), and water. Textured surfaces use the average colour of their OSRS texture.\n- **Scenery**: walls, buildings, trees, fences, rocks and the rest, turned and mirrored the way the client places them.\n- **Collision**: see [What blocks you](#what-blocks-you).\n- **Minimap**: Lumbridge's own OSRS minimap, rendered from the cache, replaces Megabonk's minimap, zoomed in 2.5x\n  towards OSRS's scale (`Minimap.Zoom`). Its map icons (trees, rocks, and map functions such as banks or altars) stay\n  upright as the minimap turns, as in OSRS.\n- **See-through walls**: see [below](#see-through-walls).\n\nMegabonk still runs the run itself. It generates the Forest stage first (its timeline, chests, shrines and boss\nportal), then Bonkscape switches the Forest's ground, props and grass off and puts Lumbridge in their place.\n\n### How it's sized\n\nThe arena is scaled to your adventurer: one OSRS tile has the same size relative to your adventurer as in OSRS. The\nadventurer is drawn larger than Megabonk's character (`Models.AdventurerScale`, 1.6 by default), and Lumbridge grows\nwith it, so there's room to run. See [Adventurers](adventurers.md#size).\n\n### When it's built\n\n1. While the main menu loads, the arena's meshes, colliders and minimap are prepared in the background from your cache.\n2. When a run starts, Bonkscape waits 1.5 s, then for Megabonk's spawn intro to finish (your character on the ground\n   and done teleporting, at most 8 s more), and places Lumbridge under you.\n3. You're moved into the courtyard, and any monster already alive is moved next to you.\n\n### Spawn, chests, shrines and the boss portal\n\n| What | Where |\n|---|---|\n| **You** | The castle courtyard, OSRS tile (3222, 3218), facing west towards the castle keep. |\n| **Chests (caskets) and shrines** | Random open ground: a walkable tile that has no roof, at least 3 tiles in from the edge, at least 6 tiles from the spawn and 3 tiles from each other. They're placed again every run. |\n| **Boss portal** | The dark hole in Lumbridge Swamp, OSRS tile (3169, 3172), the way down to the Lumbridge Swamp Caves in OSRS. |\n| **Monster spawns** | Anywhere on the arena (Megabonk's spawn area is set to the arena, minus a 2-tile margin). |\n| **Skilling spots** | On Lumbridge's own trees, rocks and shores ([Skilling](skilling.md)). |\n\nIf you ever fall through the world (25 m below Lumbridge's lowest ground), you're put back in the courtyard.\n\n### What blocks you\n\nMegabonk needs room to run, so less blocks you than in OSRS:\n\n- **Blocks**: building walls, scenery that's 2 x 2 tiles or bigger, tree trunks (thin, so you can run between trees),\n  and water, except on bridges.\n- **Doesn't block**: fences, railings, hedges, stiles, gates, doors, curtains, ladders, stairs, bushes, plants,\n  flowers, crates, barrels, sacks, tables, chairs, stools, benches, signs, and any other 1 x 1 clutter.\n\nYou and the monsters bump into these, but Megabonk's camera, its spawn checks and **projectiles pass through them**.\nMonsters find their way around walls on Lumbridge's tile grid ([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#how-monsters-move)).\n\n### See-through walls\n\nOSRS's camera looks into rooms from above; Megabonk's sits behind your shoulder. So Lumbridge's walls are split into\ncells of 8 x 8 tiles, and every frame any wall cell between Megabonk's player camera and your adventurer is hidden.\nIt stays solid while hidden.\n\n### Stages\n\nMegabonk's Forest map has several stages. Bonkscape names them **Lumbridge & Swamp**, **Lumbridge Swamp** and\n**Lumbridge Swamp Caves**, but for now every stage builds the same Lumbridge arena.\n\n## When Lumbridge isn't built\n\nYou get Megabonk's Forest instead, dressed in OSRS scenery, when:\n\n- the `Map.RealLumbridge` setting is off ([Settings](settings.md)),\n- your cache is missing any of Lumbridge's 16 map regions (the log says *\"Lumbridge isn't in this OSRS cache\"*), or\n- building it failed for any other reason (logged as *\"Lumbridge arena failed, keeping Megabonk's stage\"*).\n\nIn the Forest fallback, Megabonk's trees, rocks and bushes are drawn with OSRS models (Tree, with an Oak tree about 30%\nof the time; Tin rocks; Bush) at sensible sizes, and they keep Megabonk's own colliders. Skilling spots are placed\naround where you start: 10 trees, 8 rocks and 4 fishing spots, 12 to 70 m away.\n\n## Planned maps\n\nThese are designed in `sheets/maps.json` but **not built**:\n\n<!-- gen:maps -->\n| Map | Megabonk map | OSRS area (x0, y0, x1, y1) | Music (planned) | Minutes | Special rule | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Lumbridge & Swamp** | Forest stage 0 | 3140, 3140, 3266, 3300 | Harmony | 10 | none | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Barrows crypts** | Desert stage 0 | - | Dangerous Way | 10 | none | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **The Wilderness** | Graveyard stage 0 | - | Wilderness | 12 | skull | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **God Wars Dungeon** | Desert stage 1 | - | Armadyl Alliance | 10 | none | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 3)</span> |\n| **Fight Caves** | Desert stage 2 | - | TzHaar! | 10 | none | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 3)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:maps -->\n\nMusic per map is planned too: it needs an OSRS music synthesiser, which doesn't exist yet, so Megabonk's own music plays\neverywhere. Underground and instanced arenas (caves, dungeons, boss rooms) are on the [docket](../dev/docket.md).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Arena.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/MapProps.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skilling.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Osrs.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Runner.cs src/Bonkscape.Cache/World/ sheets/maps.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "monsters-and-bosses", "text": "# Monsters and bosses\n\n## How a monster is made\n\nEach OSRS monster takes over one or more Megabonk enemies: their spawn slots, movement and attacks. Bonkscape draws\nit with its **OSRS NPC model** from your cache, in the first frame of its standing animation, lit the way the OSRS\nclient lights it. Megabonk's own model is hidden. The OSRS model follows the enemy, feet on the ground, and turns to\nface you. Monsters aren't animated yet: no walking, attacking or dying moves.\n\nFor ordinary monsters, Bonkscape also replaces Megabonk's **HP, damage, speed and knockback resistance** with the\nrow's values. **Minibosses and bosses keep Megabonk's own stats**, so the Giant Mole fights with the HP and damage of\nthe Megabonk boss it replaces, not the sheet's 9000 HP. Megabonk enemies that no row takes over are removed from the\nForest's spawn pool, so only OSRS monsters spawn in Lumbridge.\n\n## Roster\n\n<!-- gen:enemies -->\n| Monster | OSRS NPC (id) | Stand-in NPC ids | Combat | Style | Megabonk enemies | HP | Damage | Speed | Knockback resist | Size x | Maps | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Chicken** | Chicken (1173) | 1174, 2804, 2805, 1175 | 1 | melee | Slime | 6 | 8 | 6.5 | 0 | 1 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Goblin** | Goblin (3031) | 3029, 655, 657, 659, 674, 2484 | 2 | melee | Goblin, GoblinStrong | 7 | 15 | 5 | 0 | 1 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Giant rat** | Giant rat (2510) | 2511, 2512, 2856, 2492, 1020 | 3 | melee | Ghoul | 9 | 12 | 9 | 0 | 1 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Guard** | Guard (3010) | 3011, 1546, 1547, 1548, 995, 397 | 21 | ranged | Skeleton | 20 | 20 | 5.5 | 0.1 | 1 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Cow** | Cow (2790) | 2791, 2793, 2795 | 2 | melee | ArmoredSkeleton, GoblinTank, MinibossPig | 30 | 22 | 4 | 0.3 | 1.1 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Giant frog** | Giant frog (477) | 478 | 99 | magic | Golem, MinibossGolem | 20 | 20 | 5 | 0.2 | 1.6 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Giant Mole** | Giant Mole (5779) | 6499 | 230 | melee | Ent1, Ent2, Ent3 | 9000 | 40 | 7 | 1 | 2.2 | lumbridge | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ahrim the Blighted** | Ahrim the Blighted (1672) | - | 98 | magic | MummyAncient | 70 | 40 | 5 | 0.5 | 1 | barrows | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Green dragon** | Green dragon (260) | 261, 262, 263, 264 | 79 | magic | MummyTank | 45 | 30 | 5 | 0.4 | 1 | wilderness | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Revenant imp** | Revenant imp (7881) | - | 7 | magic | Wisp | 8 | 13 | 7.5 | 0 | 1 | wilderness | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **TzTok-Jad** | TzTok-Jad (3127) | - | 702 | magic | Pharaoh1 | 8000 | 60 | 3 | 1 | 1 | fight_caves | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 3)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:enemies -->\n\nThe **Combat** column is the monster's OSRS combat level. It isn't used in play yet, and neither are the sheet's\nper-monster XP value and drop table: XP comes from the damage you deal ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md)) and every monster\ndrops the same things ([Loot](#loot)).\n\n## Combat styles\n\nEvery monster fights in **melee**, **ranged** or **magic**. In Lumbridge only the guards are ranged and only the giant\nfrogs are magic; the rest are melee. The OSRS skill icon for its style (Attack, Ranged or Magic) floats over the 10\nnearest monsters, so you know which [protection prayer](prayer.md) to use. The style is the monster's, not its\nattack's: a guard's hit counts as ranged even when Megabonk has it attack up close.\n\n## When monsters come\n\n<!-- gen:waves -->\n| Map | Minute | Monsters | Event | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| lumbridge | 0 | Chicken, Goblin, Giant rat, Guard | start | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| lumbridge | 1.5 | Cow, Giant frog | unlock | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| lumbridge | 3 | Giant frog, Cow | miniboss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| lumbridge | 4 | Goblin | swarm | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| lumbridge | 7 | Giant rat | swarm | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| lumbridge | 8 | Cow, Giant frog | miniboss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| lumbridge | 10 | Giant Mole | boss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:waves -->\n\nHow those rows apply:\n\n- **Minute 0 (start)**: chickens, goblins, giant rats and guards are the run's first monsters.\n- **Minute 1.5 (unlock)**: cows and giant frogs join the spawn pool after 90 seconds.\n- **Minutes 4 and 7 (swarm)**: Megabonk's swarm events at those minutes spawn goblins, then giant rats.\n- **Minibosses and the boss** come from Megabonk's own timeline: its miniboss slots are a Cow and a Giant frog, and\n  its stage boss is the Giant Mole. The minutes in the miniboss and boss rows are the design plan; Megabonk decides\n  when they actually arrive. Megabonk's own pacing decides how many monsters spawn and how fast.\n\n## Stand-ins\n\nYour OSRS client downloads a model the first time it shows it, so your cache may not have every monster. For each\nmonster Bonkscape tries its own NPC first, then each **stand-in NPC id** in the order listed, and uses the first one\nwhose models are all in your cache (the log says *\"Goblin: NPC 3031 isn't in this cache, using stand-in NPC 3029\"*).\nIf none is there, the monster borrows the map's fallback monster (the Goblin). If that's missing too, you see\nMegabonk's own model.\n\nTurn stand-ins off with `OSRS.UseStandIns = false` ([Settings](settings.md)).\n\n## Size\n\nA monster's height is worked out when it spawns, and once more a moment later:\n\n1. **OSRS proportions on your adventurer's scale**: its model height in OSRS units, converted to metres exactly like\n   your adventurer's. So an OSRS human (a guard) stands about as tall as your adventurer, and every other monster keeps\n   its OSRS ratio to them.\n2. Times the row's **Size x** (Cow 1.1, Giant frog 1.6, Giant Mole 2.2) and `Models.MonsterSize`.\n3. Times part of Megabonk's own enlargement of elites, minibosses and bosses, capped by tier (below). Megabonk\n   enlarges them a moment after they spawn, so this is applied again once the monster's hitbox is live.\n4. Optionally, at least a share of its Megabonk hitbox's height (`Models.MinHitboxShare`). **Off by default**:\n   Megabonk's hitboxes are tall capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton), and drawing monsters to fit them undoes the OSRS\n   proportions.\n5. Never taller than its tier's ceiling, measured against your adventurer.\n\n| Tier | Megabonk enlargement passed on, at most | Tallest, as a multiple of your adventurer |\n|---|---|---|\n| Normal | 1.15 x | 1.1 x |\n| Elite | 1.4 x | 1.35 x |\n| Miniboss | 1.6 x | 1.7 x |\n| Boss | 2.0 x | 2.2 x (`Models.BossMaxHeight`) |\n\nModel heights in OSRS units, before step 2, as the main session measured them from the cache (the standing model with\nthe NPC definition's width and height scale): Warrior 216, Guard 201, Cow 153, Giant Mole 150, Goblin 129 (0.64 of a\nguard), Giant rat 125, Giant frog 85, Chicken 79. How big they look next to each other in a run is\n*(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*.\n\nA monster's **hitbox** is always Megabonk's; only the drawing changes, so a monster can be hit (and hit you) a little\noutside its drawn shape.\n\n## How monsters move\n\nIn Megabonk, enemies run straight at you. In Lumbridge they find their way on the **OSRS tile grid** instead, like\nOSRS monsters:\n\n- Every half second, or whenever you step onto a new tile, Bonkscape works out how many steps every tile is from you,\n  moving in 8 directions, never through a wall edge, water or big scenery. A diagonal step needs both side steps open,\n  as in OSRS.\n- Each monster heads for its neighbouring tile that is one step closer, so they go around buildings and over bridges.\n- Within 3 steps of you, or off the grid, Megabonk's own chase takes over.\n\n## The Giant Mole\n\n<!-- gen:bosses -->\n| Boss | Attacks | Phase thresholds | Pet (rate) | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Giant Mole** | Claw (melee, 0 ms telegraph, contact); Dig (melee, 1200 ms telegraph, burrow teleport every 12s) | 50% HP | Baby Mole, 1/3000 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **TzTok-Jad** | Ranged slam (ranged, 1800 ms telegraph, alternate); Magic fire (magic, 1800 ms telegraph, alternate) | 50% HP | TzRek-Jad, 1/200 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 3)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:bosses -->\n\nThe Giant Mole is Lumbridge's stage boss <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span>. You call it by using the boss portal\nat the swamp's dark hole ([Maps](maps.md)). It attacks with Megabonk's own boss attacks, and Bonkscape adds its\n**dig**:\n\n1. Every **12 seconds** the chat box says *\"The Giant Mole burrows into the ground!\"* and it sinks into the ground\n   over 1.2 s.\n2. Halfway through, it moves next to you.\n3. It rises again over the next 1.2 s.\n\nBelow **50% HP** it digs more often, every 8 seconds.\n\nPlanned for the Mole: its own drops (Mole claw, the Baby mole pet at 1/3000) and a real Mole lair fight. Neither is\nbuilt.\n\n## Loot\n\nMonsters drop Megabonk's normal pickups, dressed as OSRS items, plus Bonkscape's own prayer potions:\n\n| Drop | What it is | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Coins** | Megabonk's gold, drawn as the OSRS coin stack for the amount (1 coin up to the big pile) | Megabonk's gold |\n| **Shrimps** (60%), **Lobster** (30%), **Shark** (10%) | Megabonk's health pickup, as a random OSRS food | Heals 15, 30 or 60 HP in place of Megabonk's amount: *\"You eat the shrimps. It heals some health.\"* |\n| **Prayer potion(4)** | Bonkscape's own pickup, 2.5% chance per kill | Restores prayer points ([Prayer](prayer.md#prayer-potions)) |\n| **Casket** | Megabonk's chest | Megabonk's chest reward, and [evolutions](weapons-and-evolutions.md#evolutions) |\n\nThe sheet also plans a rare clue scroll (easy) drop, the Mole claw and the Baby mole; none of those is built.\n\n## Planned monsters\n\nAhrim the Blighted (Barrows), green dragons and revenant imps (the Wilderness) and TzTok-Jad (the Fight Caves) are in\nthe roster above as planned rows for the planned maps. None of them spawns yet.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/EnemySkins.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Bosses.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Pathing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Loot.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Sizing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Osrs.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Rows.cs sheets/enemies.json sheets/bosses.json sheets/waves.json sheets/drops.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "prayer", "text": "# Prayer\n\nEvery monster fights in one combat style (melee, ranged or magic), shown by the icon over the nearest monsters. A\n**protection prayer** against that style blocks its hits. <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span>\n\n<!-- gen:prayers -->\n| Prayer | Blocks | Normal monsters | Bosses | Drain (points/s) | Default key | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Protect from Melee** | melee | 100% | 50% | 0.333 | 1 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Protect from Missiles** | ranged | 100% | 50% | 0.333 | 2 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Protect from Magic** | magic | 100% | 50% | 0.333 | 3 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n<!-- /gen:prayers -->\n\n## Using prayers\n\n- Press **1**, **2** or **3** to turn on Protect from Melee, Missiles or Magic. Change the keys with `Prayer.Keys`\n  ([Settings](settings.md)).\n- **One at a time**: turning one on replaces the one that was on. Press its key again to turn it off.\n- Each prayer plays its OSRS sound when it goes on, and the prayer-off sound when you turn it off.\n- The keys do nothing while you're typing in Megabonk's chat.\n- While a prayer is on, its OSRS **overhead icon** floats above your adventurer.\n\n## What it blocks\n\nWhen a monster hits you and your prayer matches **that monster's style**:\n\n| Monster | Damage blocked |\n|---|---|\n| Bosses (anything Megabonk flags as a boss, stage boss or final boss, such as the Giant Mole) | **50%** |\n| Every other monster | **100%**: the hit shows as a blue 0 hitsplat |\n\nWhether Megabonk flags its minibosses (the Cow and Giant frog minibosses) as bosses hasn't been checked yet.\n\n*\"Protected!\"* flashes over your adventurer whenever the prayer stops (or halves) a hit. Hits from a style you're not\npraying against go through in full.\n\n## Prayer points\n\n- You start every run with **20 + your Prayer level** points (21 at Prayer 1, 119 at 99).\n- An active prayer drains **0.333 points a second**, one point every 3 seconds.\n- While a prayer is on you earn **2 Prayer XP a second** ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md)), so a higher Prayer level means\n  more points in later runs.\n- At 0 points the prayer switches off with OSRS's empty-prayer sound and the chat says *\"You have run out of Prayer\n  points, you can recharge at an altar.\"* Pressing a key with no points left says *\"You need to recharge your Prayer\n  at an altar.\"* There's no altar in Lumbridge yet: potions are the only way back.\n\n## Prayer potions\n\nEach kill has a **2.5%** chance to drop a **Prayer potion(4)**. It spins on the ground, slides towards you once you're\nwithin about 9 m, and you drink it when you get close: **7 points + 25% of your maximum**, *\"You drink some of your\nprayer potion.\"*\n\n## The prayer panel\n\nAt the bottom right of the screen, on a small OSRS stone panel: the three protection prayer icons as in OSRS's prayer\nbook, each with its key under it. The active one sits on OSRS's yellow glow and its key turns yellow. When you're out\nof points, the prayers that aren't on are dimmed.\n\nYour prayer points are on the **prayer orb** beside the minimap ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#in-a-run)): the number is green\nwhen full, yellow at half and red when empty, and the orb lights up while a prayer is on.\n\nFor the first 45 seconds of a run, a hint above the panel reads *\"Pray against the icon over a monster: 1 Melee 2\nMissiles 3 Magic\"*.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Prayer.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/HudLayout.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Loot.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs sheets/prayers.json sheets/drops.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "settings", "text": "# Settings\n\nBonkscape's settings are in **`BepInEx/config/gg.melty.bonkscape.cfg`** in Megabonk's folder. BepInEx writes the file,\nwith every key at its default, the first time Megabonk starts with Bonkscape. Edit it with Megabonk closed: settings\nare read once, when the game starts. For the `Models`, `Camera` and `Minimap` keys, a value outside the range is clamped to the\nnearest end.\n\n| Section | Key | Default | Range | What it does |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `OSRS` | `CacheFolder` | *(empty)* | a folder | The folder holding OSRS's `main_file_cache.dat2` and `.idx` files. Empty: Bonkscape finds it ([Getting started](getting-started.md#where-bonkscape-looks-for-your-osrs-files)). |\n| `OSRS` | `UseStandIns` | `true` | true / false | When a monster's own model isn't in your cache, use the next stand-in NPC that is ([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#stand-ins)). Off: such monsters borrow the Goblin's model, or keep Megabonk's. |\n| `Models` | `AdventurerScale` | `1.6` | 0.5 to 3 | Your adventurer's height as a share of Megabonk's character (1 = the same height). Lumbridge scales with it. |\n| `Models` | `MonsterSize` | `1.0` | 0.3 to 3 | OSRS monsters' size relative to your adventurer's scale. 1 = OSRS proportions: OSRS humans (guards) about as tall as your adventurer, goblins, rats and chickens smaller. An old `MonsterScale` line is ignored. |\n| `Models` | `MinHitboxShare` | `0` | 0 to 2 | Draw monsters at least this share of their Megabonk hitbox's height, up to their size ceiling. 0 = off: Megabonk's hitboxes are tall capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton), so a floor undoes OSRS proportions. Replaced `HitboxFill` (0.85, then 0.6) in 0.1.15; an old `HitboxFill` line is ignored. |\n| `Models` | `BossMaxHeight` | `2.2` | 1 to 6 | The tallest a boss may be drawn, as a multiple of your adventurer's height. New in 0.1.13. |\n| `Camera` | `Distance` | `0.8` | 0.4 to 1.5 | Megabonk's follow camera distance (1 = Megabonk's own; lower = closer). Scales both the camera's offset (about 11 m) and the extra zoom-out it adds as hordes grow (up to about 15 m). New in 0.1.13. |\n| `Minimap` | `Zoom` | `2.5` | 1 to 6 | Zooms Megabonk's minimap in on Lumbridge (1 = Megabonk's own scale; OSRS's minimap is about 3x closer). New in 0.1.15. |\n| `Map` | `RealLumbridge` | `true` | true / false | Build the real Lumbridge from your cache as the arena. Off: Megabonk's Forest with OSRS scenery ([Maps](maps.md#when-lumbridge-isnt-built)). |\n| `Audio` | `OsrsVolume` | `0.55` | 0 to 1 | Volume of OSRS sound effects (0 = silent). Not clamped, so keep it in range. |\n| `Prayer` | `Keys` | `Alpha1,Alpha2,Alpha3` | three Unity key names | Keys for Protect from Melee, Missiles and Magic, comma-separated, as Unity `KeyCode` names: `Alpha1` is the 1 key above the letters, `Keypad1` the number pad's, `Z`, `X`, `C` letters. A name Unity doesn't know keeps that prayer's default. |\n| `Dev` | `DumpData` | `false` | true / false | Writes Megabonk's loaded data (weapons, tomes, enemies, maps, characters, music) to `BepInEx/config/Bonkscape/dump.json`. For development. |\n| `Debug` | `HideMegabonkHud` | `true` | true / false | Hide Megabonk's own health bar, XP bar and monster health bars, which the OSRS HUD replaces. Off: the OSRS HUD is still drawn, Megabonk's bars stay up beside it, and Bonkscape doesn't read Megabonk's XP bar. For tracking down problems. |\n| `Debug` | `OsrsHud` | `true` | true / false | Draw Bonkscape's OSRS HUD. Off: no HUD is drawn, its interface sprites aren't loaded, and Megabonk's own HUD stays as it is. For tracking down problems. |\n| `Dev` | `AutoStartRun` | `false` | true / false | Starts a Lumbridge run with autoplay by itself, the way Melty's test does ([Testing](../dev/testing.md)). For development. |\n\nThe camera distance is applied at the start of every stage. The `Models` settings decide sizes when a run starts and\nwhen each monster spawns.\n\n## Other files\n\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\skills.json` | Your skills' XP ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md#saving)) |\n| `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\settings.properties` | Read if present: `OSRS_DIR=` (the OSRS folder Melty passes in) and `OSRS_CACHE=` (a cache folder, used when `OSRS.CacheFolder` is empty) |\n| `BepInEx/LogOutput.log` | BepInEx's log, with Bonkscape's lines |\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/CameraTweak.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Sizing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Dev/DataDump.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "skilling", "text": "# Skilling\n\nLumbridge's own trees, rocks and shores are skilling spots. <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span>\n\n## How to gather\n\nStand next to a spot for **1.2 seconds**. Walking out of reach resets the timer. There's no button, no tool and no\nlevel requirement: being close is enough, so you can skill while you fight.\n\n| Spot | How many | Reach | Reward | XP | Back after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Tree** (Lumbridge's trees and oaks) | 14 | about 1.8 tiles | **25 coins** and Megabonk's **Haste** speed boost. *\"You get some logs.\"* | 25 Woodcutting | 30 s |\n| **Rocks** | 10 | about 1.6 tiles | Megabonk's **Shield**. *\"You manage to mine some copper.\"* | 17.5 Mining | 30 s |\n| **Fishing spot** (on the water by the shore) | 6 | about 1.6 tiles | **Heals 20 HP**. *\"You catch some shrimps.\"* | 10 Fishing | 20 s |\n\nThe Haste and Shield are the same effects as Megabonk's own Haste and Shield pickups. Each spot plays an OSRS sound\nwhen you gather from it.\n\n## Where the spots are\n\n- **Trees and rocks** are real Lumbridge objects: 14 of the objects named *Tree* or *Oak* and 10 named *Rocks* are\n  picked as spots. They're the same ones every run. They look like every other tree and rock, and nothing marks which\n  ones are spots yet.\n- **Fishing spots** are 6 water tiles next to walkable shore, on the River Lum and in the swamp. Each shows OSRS's\n  fishing spot model on the water and disappears while it's used up.\n\nA used-up tree or rock looks the same; it just gives nothing until it's back.\n\nIn the Forest fallback ([Maps](maps.md#when-lumbridge-isnt-built)) the spots are OSRS models placed around where you\nstart: 10 trees, 8 rocks and 4 fishing spots.\n\n## The sheet and the code\n\nThe drops sheet describes the rewards a little differently from what runs:\n\n| Sheet row | Sheet effect | What the code does |\n|---|---|---|\n| Logs | `gold:25;speed:0.2:6` (25 coins, +20% speed for 6 s) | 25 coins and Megabonk's Haste effect |\n| Copper ore | `armor:0.15:8` (+15% armour for 8 s) | Megabonk's Shield effect |\n| Raw shrimps | `heal:20` | Heals 20 |\n\nThe arena places 14/10/6 spots; the map row's counts (10/8/4) and respawn times are used by the Forest fallback, and\nthe respawn times by both.\n\nGathering levels don't change any reward yet.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skilling.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Arena.cs sheets/maps.json sheets/drops.json sheets/skills.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "skills-and-xp", "text": "# Skills and XP\n\nBonkscape has ten OSRS skills. They're **kept between runs** and use OSRS's real 1-99 XP table.\n<span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> (XP drops and level-ups seen in Melty test runs).\n\n<!-- gen:skills -->\n| Skill | Trained by (sheet) | XP rate | Starting weapon unlocks | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Attack** | `melee_damage:accurate` | 0.25 | 70: Abyssal whip | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Strength** | `melee_damage:aggressive` | 0.25 | - | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Defence** | `melee_damage:defensive` | 0.25 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ranged** | `ranged_damage` | 0.25 | 55: Red chinchompa, 75: Toxic blowpipe | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Magic** | `magic_damage` | 0.25 | 75: Trident of the seas, 94: Ice Barrage | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Hitpoints** | `any_damage:third` | 0.0833 | - | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Prayer** | `seconds_praying` | 2 | - | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Woodcutting** | `node:tree` | 25 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Mining** | `node:rock` | 17.5 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Fishing** | `node:fishing` | 10 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:skills -->\n\n## The XP table\n\nThe same formula as OSRS: level *L* needs \u230a(1/4) \u00d7 \u03a3 from *l* = 1 to *L* \u2212 1 of \u230a*l* + 300 \u00d7 2^(*l*/7)\u230b\u230b XP.\n\n| Level | XP | Level | XP |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 83 | 60 | 273,742 |\n| 10 | 1,154 | 70 | 737,627 |\n| 20 | 4,470 | 75 | 1,210,421 |\n| 30 | 13,363 | 80 | 1,986,068 |\n| 40 | 37,224 | 90 | 5,346,332 |\n| 50 | 101,333 | 99 | 13,034,431 |\n\nXP keeps counting past 99, up to 200,000,000 per skill. **Hitpoints starts at level 10** (1,154 XP), as in OSRS;\nevery other skill starts at 1.\n\n## What trains what\n\n**Combat skills** get XP for the damage you actually deal: the HP a monster loses, not the number Megabonk rolled.\n\n| You deal damage with | Trains | XP per point of damage |\n|---|---|---|\n| A melee weapon, as an *accurate* adventurer (Ranger, Mage) | Attack | 0.25 |\n| A melee weapon, as an *aggressive* adventurer (Warrior) | Strength | 0.25 |\n| A melee weapon, as a *defensive* adventurer (none yet) | Defence | 0.25 |\n| A ranged weapon (any adventurer) | Ranged | 0.25 |\n| A magic weapon (any adventurer) | Magic | 0.25 |\n| Any weapon | Hitpoints, as well | 0.0833 (a third) |\n\nThe weapon's style decides ranged and magic; for melee weapons your adventurer's attack style picks the skill. So:\n\n- the Warrior trains **Strength** (and Hitpoints) with melee weapons;\n- **Attack** only goes up when the Ranger or Mage deals damage with a melee weapon taken on level-up;\n- **Defence** can't be trained yet: no phase-1 adventurer fights defensively (the planned Ironman does).\n\n**Prayer** gets 2 XP for every second a protection prayer is on. **Gathering skills** get a fixed amount per action:\nWoodcutting 25, Mining 17.5 and Fishing 10 ([Skilling](skilling.md)).\n\n## XP drops and level-ups\n\n- XP is grouped per OSRS game tick (0.6 s) and per skill. Each group is an OSRS **XP drop**, the skill icon and the\n  amount, rising into the **XP counter** beside the minimap, which shows your total XP over all skills\n  ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#in-a-run)).\n- On a level-up, the chat box says *\"Congratulations, you just advanced a Strength level. You are now level 41.\"* and\n  OSRS's level-up sound plays. OSRS's level-up dialogue then covers the chat box for 3 s (*\"Congratulations, you just\n  advanced a Strength level.\"*, *\"Your Strength level is now 41.\"*) and OSRS's level-up fireworks play at your feet.\n  (OSRS's level-up jingle is planned; it needs the music synthesiser.)\n\n## Unlocks by level\n\nSkill levels unlock better **starting weapons** ([Adventurers](adventurers.md#starting-weapons)):\n\n| Skill | Level | Starting weapon |\n|---|---|---|\n| Attack | 70 | Abyssal whip (Warrior) |\n| Ranged | 55 | Red chinchompa (Ranger) |\n| Ranged | 75 | Toxic blowpipe (Ranger) |\n| Magic | 75 | Trident of the seas (Mage) |\n| Magic | 94 | Ice Barrage (Mage) |\n\nYour Prayer level also raises your prayer points (20 + level). The planned Pure and Ironman adventurers have level\nconditions too (*1 Defence, 60 Attack* and *total level 250*); they aren't built.\n\n## Combat level\n\nThe character select panel shows your **combat level**, worked out with OSRS's formula:\n\n- base = \u00bc \u00d7 (Defence + Hitpoints + \u230aPrayer / 2\u230b)\n- melee = 0.325 \u00d7 (Attack + Strength), ranged = 0.325 \u00d7 \u230a1.5 \u00d7 Ranged\u230b, magic = 0.325 \u00d7 \u230a1.5 \u00d7 Magic\u230b\n- combat level = \u230abase + the biggest of melee, ranged and magic\u230b\n\nA fresh save (10 Hitpoints, everything else 1) is combat level 3. Combat level doesn't affect play.\n\n## Saving\n\nSkills are saved to **`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\skills.json`**, a plain list of each skill's XP. Bonkscape saves when\nanything changed, every 20 seconds, at the end of a run and when you quit Megabonk. If the file can't be read, you\nstart fresh (the log says *\"skills save unreadable, starting fresh\"*). To reset your skills, delete the file while\nMegabonk is closed.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skills.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Prayer.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skilling.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/CharacterSelect.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/HudLayout.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/LevelUpFx.cs sheets/skills.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "weapons-and-evolutions", "text": "# Weapons and evolutions\n\n## How a Bonkscape weapon works\n\nEvery OSRS weapon takes over one Megabonk weapon (its *Megabonk base*). It keeps that weapon's **behaviour**: how it\nattacks, its projectile and its visuals. Bonkscape replaces the rest:\n\n- **Base stats**: damage, cooldown, area, amount (projectiles), speed (projectile speed), bounces, duration and\n  knockback come from the row below.\n- **Level-up upgrades**: the weapon's Megabonk upgrade pool is replaced with the row's list.\n- **Name and icon**: the OSRS name, and an icon rendered from your cache. Fire Strike, Ice Barrage and Fire Surge use\n  their OSRS spell icons; the rest use the item's inventory icon.\n\nIn Lumbridge, level-ups offer only these eight weapons, and they all count as unlocked whatever your Megabonk progress\nis. What you see and hear when a weapon fires is still Megabonk's: the OSRS projectiles and weapon sounds listed in\nthe sheet aren't used yet.\n\n## Weapons\n\n<!-- gen:weapons -->\n| Weapon | OSRS item | Style | Megabonk base | Damage | Cooldown | Area | Amount | Speed | Bounces | Duration | Knockback | Skill levels to start a run with it | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Abyssal whip** | Abyssal whip | melee | Katana | 10 | 0.35 | 1.15 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0.5 | 1 | 70 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dragon scimitar** | Dragon scimitar | melee | Sword | 11 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | none (a starting weapon) | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Magic shortbow** | Magic shortbow | ranged | Bow | 8 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | none (a starting weapon) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Toxic blowpipe** | Toxic blowpipe | ranged | Revolver | 4 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 2.2 | 0 | 1 | 0.4 | 75 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Fire Strike** | Staff of fire | magic | FireStaff | 10 | 0.5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 2 | 1 | none (a starting weapon) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ice Barrage** | Ancient staff | magic | Frostwalker | 9 | 1.25 | 1.1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1.6 | 0.5 | 94 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Trident of the seas** | Trident of the Seas | magic | LightningStaff | 8 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 75 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Red chinchompa** | Red chinchompa | ranged | Rockets | 11 | 0.35 | 1.2 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 5 | 2 | 55 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dwarf multicannon** | Cannon base | ranged | new: deployable | 6 | 4 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 10 | 0.5 | 1 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Dharok's greataxe** | Dharok's greataxe | melee | Axe | 14 | 1.6 | 1.3 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 0.82 | 2 | 70 Attack, 70 Strength | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Scythe of vitur** | Scythe of Vitur | melee | Scythe | 12 | 0.85 | 1.4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 1 | 80 Attack, 90 Strength | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Armadyl godsword** | Armadyl godsword | melee | HeroSword | 16 | 1.2 | 1.3 | 1 | 30 | 0 | 0.5 | 3 | 75 Attack | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Dragon claws** | Dragon claws | melee | Dexecutioner | 9 | 0.6 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 1 | 60 Attack | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:weapons -->\n\n\"Skill levels to start a run with it\" only matters for the **starting** weapon\n([Adventurers](adventurers.md#starting-weapons)). Any weapon can turn up as a level-up offer.\n\nEach weapon trains a skill when it deals damage: melee weapons train Attack, Strength or Defence (by your\nadventurer's attack style), ranged weapons Ranged, magic weapons Magic, and all of them some Hitpoints\n([Skills and XP](skills-and-xp.md)).\n\n### Level-ups and special attacks\n\nWhen a weapon levels up, Megabonk offers upgrades from its pool. Bonkscape's pools:\n\n<!-- gen:weapon-levels -->\n| Weapon | Level-up upgrade pool | Special attack | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Abyssal whip** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack speed +0.08 (addition); attack size +0.15 (addition); crit chance +0.06 (flat) | Energy Drain (not built) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dragon scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (not built) | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Magic shortbow** | damage +1.6 (flat); projectiles +1 (flat); projectile speed +0.2 (addition); crit chance +0.08 (flat) | Snapshot (not built) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Toxic blowpipe** | damage +2.0 (flat); projectiles +1 (flat); crit chance +0.08 (flat); projectile speed +0.2 (addition) | Toxic Siphon (not built) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Fire Strike** | damage +2.5 (flat); projectiles +1 (flat); projectile speed +0.2 (addition); attack size +0.16 (addition) | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ice Barrage** | attack size +0.12 (addition); damage +2.0 (flat); duration +0.12 (flat) | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Trident of the seas** | damage +2.0 (flat); projectiles +1 (flat); bounces +1 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition) | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Red chinchompa** | damage +2.0 (flat); projectiles +1 (flat); projectile speed +0.2 (addition); attack size +0.15 (addition) | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dwarf multicannon** | damage +1.5 (flat); attack speed +0.1 (addition); duration +0.2 (flat) | - | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Dharok's greataxe** | damage +3.0 (flat); attack size +0.15 (addition) | Wretched Strength (damage x missing hp, not built) | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Scythe of vitur** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition) | - | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Armadyl godsword** | damage +3.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition) | The Judgement (godsword smash, not built) | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Dragon claws** | damage +2.0 (flat); crit chance +0.08 (flat) | Slice and Dice (four hit burst, not built) | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:weapon-levels -->\n\nSpecial attacks are named in the sheet but **not built**: there's no special attack bar.\n\n## Caskets\n\nMegabonk's chests wear the OSRS **Casket** model, and their map icon stays. Opening one gives Megabonk's normal chest\nreward. Opening a casket is also when evolutions happen.\n\n## Evolutions\n\nAn evolution turns a maxed weapon into its OSRS upgrade. When you open a casket, Bonkscape checks every evolution:\n\n1. You have its weapon at **level 8 or higher**, and\n2. you hold its **gear passive** (any level).\n\nIf both are true, the weapon evolves on the spot: its base stats are multiplied as below, it takes the new name and\nicon, the chat box says *\"Your Abyssal whip has become an Abyssal tentacle!\"*, a banner shows the new name, and\nOSRS's level-up sound plays. Each evolution happens once per run, and every run starts with the plain weapons again.\n\n<!-- gen:evolutions -->\n| Becomes | Weapon | + gear passive | Weapon level | Stat changes | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Abyssal tentacle** | Abyssal whip | Kraken tentacle | 8 | damage x1.5, attack speed x1.2, attack size x1.25 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Fire Surge** | Fire Strike | Tome of fire | 8 | damage x1.8, projectiles x1, attack size x1.3 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Armadyl godsword (i)** | Armadyl godsword | Godsword shard | 8 | damage x1.5 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n| **Infernal cape** | any weapon | Fire cape | 1 | damage x1.1 | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 2)</span> |\n<!-- /gen:evolutions -->\n\nFire Surge's \"projectiles x1\" leaves the number of projectiles as it was.\n\nTo aim for one: take the **Abyssal whip** with the **Kraken tentacle**, or **Fire Strike** with the **Tome of fire**\n([Gear passives](gear-passives.md)), level the weapon to 8, then open a casket.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Evolutions.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Loot.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs sheets/weapons.json sheets/evolutions.json -->\n"}]